1 NOTE {geni:about_me} =Prince Frederick Adolf, Duke of Östergötland=
2 CONT
2 CONT [https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Prince_Frederick_Adolf,_Duke_of_%C3%96sterg%C3%B6tland '''Prince Frederick Adolf, Duke of Östergötland'''] was a Swedish Prince, youngest son of [https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Adolf_Frederick,_King_o
2 CONC f_Sweden '''King Adolf Frederick of Sweden'''] and [https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Louisa_Ulrika_of_Prussia '''Louisa Ulrika of Prussia'''], a sister of [https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Frederick_the_Great '''Frederick the Great'''],
2 CONC  King of Prussia. He was given the title [https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/List_of_dukes_and_duchesses_of_%C3%96sterg%C3%B6tland '''Duke of Östergötland'''].
2 CONT
2 CONT ===Life===
2 CONT
2 CONT '''During his childhood''', Frederick Adolf was under the tutelage of [https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Ulrica_Sch%C3%B6nstr%C3%B6m '''Ulrica Schönström''']. The Duke was described as "''the most beautiful Prince in Europe''" and was
2 CONC  described as sensitive and spoiled by his mother. He and his sister, [https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Sophia_Albertina,_Abbess_of_Quedlinburg '''Sophia Albertina'''], were their mother's favourites and also devoted to each other. D
2 CONC uring family conflicts, such as the famous succession scandal regarding the questioned legitimacy of the Crown Prince in 1778, he and his sister were on their mother's side against that of their brothers Charles and Gustav. As a c
2 CONC hild, he had a weak health and a fierce temperament. His education became somewhat lacking.
2 CONT
2 CONT '''Frederik was made''' colonel in 1762, general major in 1768, general lieutenant in 1774, commander of the Västmanland regiment in 1775 and field marshal in 1792. He was given a minor role in the [https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/R
2 CONC evolution_of_1772 Revolution of 1772] of his brother [https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Gustav_III '''Gustav III'''], who gave him the task of agitating in Södermanland and Östergötland.
2 CONT
2 CONT ===Reign of Gustav III===
2 CONT
2 CONT '''He was given the title''' Duke of Östergötland on 8 September 1772 and the [https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Tullgarn_Palace '''Tullgarn Palace'''] as his residence.
2 CONT
2 CONT '''During the great''' succession scandal, the so-called Munck Affair in 1778, when the queen dowager Louisa Ulrika questioned the legitimacy of the Crown prince in reference to the rumors that Gustav III had convinced [https://en
2 CONC .wikipedia.org/wiki/Adolf_Fredrik_Munck '''Adolf Fredrik Munck'''] to impregnate the queen, [https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Sophia_Magdalena_of_Denmark '''Sophia Magdalena of Denmark'''], Frederick sided with his mother and defende
2 CONC d her before the king by pointing out that these rumors had not been invented by their mother but were in fact widespread rumors, and he reportedly said to his brother the king: "''The entire city is talking of it, and it is commo
2 CONC nly believed that You are not altogether man, and that it is because of this reason, that You have enticed the Queen to it to have an heir to the Kingdom''." It was Frederick who convinced Louisa Ulrika to receive Gustav III on he
2 CONC r deathbed in 1782, thereby accomplishing peace between them.
2 CONT
2 CONT '''His sister-in-law''', [https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Hedvig_Elisabeth_Charlotte_of_Holstein-Gottorp '''Hedwig Elizabeth Charlotte of Holstein-Gottorp'''], describes him as beautiful, with expressive eyes, an easygoing temper, a
2 CONC nd very handsome when he dresses properly, though often badly dressed in his private life, and gives the estimation that he would have been a greater social success, if he did not say so many suggestive things and had such a filth
2 CONC y mouth [that is to say, he used a sexually suggestive language], which he acquired because he had spent too much time with men, and had such a weakness for women and sex. 
2 CONT
2 CONT '''He had no tasks in his''' life other than the ceremonial, and spent his life wasting money and involving himself in love affairs. Gustav III reportedly had no high opinion of his intellectual capacity. Frederick was an honorary
2 CONC  member of the Swedish Royal Academy of Fine Arts, and he did occasionally show a genuine interest in the affairs of the academy, as well as in the management of the Västmanland regiment. He devoted much time to country life on hi
2 CONC s estate, Tullgarn. His economic affairs were in bad shape, and in 1791 he was finally declared bankrupt and placed under administration until 1802.
2 CONT
2 CONT '''Frederick served in the''' [https://www.geni.com/projects/Kustaa-III-n-sota-1788-1790/3758734 Russo-Swedish War] in Finland in 1788. During the [https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Battle_of_Hogland Battle of Hogland], Fredrick wishe
2 CONC d to send reinforcements by fleet to aid his brother, Duke Charles. This was prevented, and Frederick left the army in protest to Gustav III, whom he referred to as a tyrant. He thereby came to belong to the opposition, and he als
2 CONC o became involved in the planned coup by his sister-in-law to depose the monarch; [https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/1789_Conspiracy_(Sweden%29 the 1789 Conspiracy]. 
2 CONT
2 CONT '''In the autumn of 1789''', Hedvig Elisabeth Charlotte prepared to depose Gustav III and place her husband Duke Charles upon the throne.[3] Her ideal was the Swedish Constitution of 1772, which she saw as a good tool for an enlig
2 CONC htened aristocracy, and the war and the Union and Security Act had made her a leading part of the opposition. She cooperated with Prince Frederick Adolf and [https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Gustaf_Adolf_Reuterholm '''Gustaf Adolf Re
2 CONC uterholm''']. The plan was to force Charles to act as a symbol of the opposition to the Union and Security Act when the time was right. When the time arrived to make Charles act, however, he refused, which effectively discontinued
2 CONC  the coup.
2 CONT
2 CONT ===Reign of Gustav IV Adolf===
2 CONT
2 CONT '''In July 1793, he was''' given the position to chair the government during the journey of the king and the regent in the southern provinces, but nothing whatsoever was apparently accomplished during his tenure, and during a simi
2 CONC lar journey in 1794, he was not entrusted again. In 1800, Frederick Adolf left Sweden for health reasons and travelled to Germany and then to France. He died in Montpellier in France in 1803.
2 CONT
2 CONT ===Private life===
2 CONT
2 CONT '''Prince Fredrick Adolf is''' in fact most known in history for his love life. He was never married, and the ceremonial duties of his consort were performed by his sister Sophia Albertina. He had several plans to marry, but none 
2 CONC of them was realised. 
2 CONT
2 CONT '''His first proposal was''' to the Countess [https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Ulla_von_H%C3%B6pken '''Ulla von Höpken'''], but she was married to another, and he accompanied his brother Gustav to France in 1770 to forget her. In 177
2 CONC 4, he proposed to the cousin of his former love, Countess [https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Sophie_Piper '''Sophie von Fersen'''], daughter of [https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Axel_von_Fersen_the_Elder '''Axel von Fersen the Elder'''] 
2 CONC and sister of [https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Axel_von_Fersen_the_Younger '''Axel von Fersen the Younger'''], the alleged lover of [https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Marie_Antoinette '''Marie Antoinette''']. She and her father refused,
2 CONC  as they were afraid that she would be badly treated by his brother and mother, who was reluctant to give their consent, and because she was already engaged, and Frederick Adolf was sent to Italy in 1776 until she was married. 
2 CONT
2 CONT '''He lived from 1778 to''' 1795, in a happy relationship with the ballet dancer [https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Sophie_Hagman '''Sophie Hagman'''], who was well liked at court, and had a daughter, Sophia Frederica, with her. In 17
2 CONC 80, he temporarily ended his relationship with Hagman and proposed to the noble Margaretha Lovisa Wrangel, with whom he became informally engaged. The King gave his permission to the marriage with the condition that it was postpon
2 CONC ed for a year, during which Wrangel was sent to Scania, with the thought that his brother would change his mind when the time was up. This was also the case, and Frederick Adolf returned to Hagman in 1781. 
2 CONT
2 CONT '''After his relationship with''' Hagman ended, he proposed to Princess [https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Princess_Augusta_Sophia_of_the_United_Kingdom '''Augusta Sophia of the United Kingdom'''] in 1797, and after his relationship w
2 CONC ith [https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Euphrosyne_L%C3%B6f '''Euphrosyne Löf'''] ended, he proposed to [https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Dorothea_von_Medem '''Dorothea von Medem'''], dowager duchess of Courland in 1801, but none of the m
2 CONC arriages was realized.
2 CONT
