2 TITL ROYAL VAULT UNDER, ST. GEORGE'S CHAPEL. Resting place of George III King of England & King George IV King of England along with many others • See list below
2 NOTE Royal Burials
3 CONT
3 CONT St George's Chapel is the resting place of many Kings and Queens, particularly since the creation of the Royal Vault, which was built by George III. At the appropriate moment in the funeral service, the coffin descends into the va
3 CONC ult below. Most Kings and Queens since George III have been buried at St George's. Members of the Royal Family have also been interred in the Royal Vault, but more recently, it has been normal to bury them in the Royal Family's Pr
3 CONC ivate Burial Ground at Frogmore in the grounds of Windsor Castle.
2 NOTE Rest Of St. George's Chapel:
3 CONT Quire:
3 CONT Henry VIII (d. 1547)
3 CONT Jane Seymour, third wife of Henry VIII (d. 1537)
3 CONT Charles I (d.1649)
3 CONT Infant child of Queen Anne (d.1696)
3 CONT North Quire Aisle:
3 CONT King Edward IV (d. 1483)
3 CONT Queen Elizabeth Woodville (d. 1492)
3 CONT Princess Louise, Duchess of Saxe-Weimar, niece of Queen Adelaide (d.1832)
3 CONT
3 CONT King George VI Memorial Chapel:
3 CONT King George VI (d.1952, buried in chapel 1969)
3 CONT Queen Elizabeth (d.2002)
3 CONT Princess Margaret, Countess of Snowdon (d.2002) (ashes)
3 CONT
3 CONT South Quire Aisle:
3 CONT King Henry VI (d.1471)
3 CONT King Edward VII (d.1910)
3 CONT Queen Alexandra (d.1925)
3 CONT
3 CONT The Gloucester Vault:
3 CONT Prince William, Duke of Gloucester (d.1805)
3 CONT Princess Maria, Duchess of Gloucester (d.1807)
3 CONT Prince William, Duke of Gloucester (d.1834)
3 CONT Princess Sophia of Gloucester (d.1844)
3 CONT Princess Mary, Duchess of Gloucester (d.1857)
3 CONT
3 CONT North Nave Aisle:
3 CONT King George V (d.1936, placed there 1939)
3 CONT Queen Mary (d.1953)
2 NOTE Buried in the Royal Vault:
3 CONT Princess Amelia, daughter of George III (d.1810)
3 CONT Princess Augusta, Duchess of Brunswick, sister of George III (d.1813)
3 CONT Stillborn son of Princess Charlotte (d. 1817)
3 CONT Princess Charlotte (daughter of George IV) (d.1817)
3 CONT Queen Charlotte, wife of George III (d.1818)
3 CONT Prince Edward, Duke of Kent, father of Queen Victoria (d.1820)
3 CONT King George III (d.1820)
3 CONT Prince Alfred, son of George III (d.1782, placed in vault 1820)
3 CONT Prince Octavius, son of George III (d.1783, placed in vault 1820)
3 CONT Princess Elizabeth, daughter of William IV (d.1821)
3 CONT Prince Frederick, Duke of York (d.1827)
3 CONT King George IV (d.1830)
3 CONT Still-born daughter of Prince Ernest Augustus, son of George III (d.1818)
3 CONT King William IV (d.1837)
3 CONT Princess Sophia, daughter of George III (d.1840)
3 CONT Queen Adelaide, wife of William IV (d.1849)
3 CONT Prince Frederick of Schleswig-Holstein, son of Princess Christian (d.1876)
3 CONT King George V of Hanover (d.1878)
3 CONT Victoria von Pawel Rammingen, daughter of Princess Frederica of Hanover (d.1881)
3 CONT Princess Mary Adelaide, Duchess of Teck, mother of Queen Mary (d.1897)
3 CONT Prince Francis, Duke of Teck, father of Queen Mary (d.1900)
3 CONT Princess Frederika of Hanover (d.1926)
3 CONT Prince Adolphus, Duke of Cambridge, grandfather of Queen Mary (d.1850, placed in vault 1930)
3 CONT Princess Augusta, Duchess of Cambridge, grandmother of Queen Mary (d.1889, placed in vault 1930)
