1 NOTE He was king under the regency of his uncle from 1792 until 1800, when he 
2 CONT was crowned. Gustav was a reactionary and despotic ruler. His hatred of 
2 CONT the French Republic prompted him to join the Third Coalition against 
2 CONT Napoleon, a move that resulted in the loss of Pomerania to France in 1807 
2 CONT and Finland to Russia in 1808. The following year the Swedish nobles 
2 CONT forced him to abdicate and adopted a charter providing for a 
2 CONT constitutional monarchy. Gustav died in exile. He was succeeded by his 
2 CONT uncle, Charles XIII.
