1 NOTE {geni:about_me} [https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Auguste_Sophie_Friederike_of_Hesse-Kassel '''Auguste Sophie Friederike Marie Caroline Julie of Hesse-Kassel'''], known as Princess Augusta, was a Princess of [https://en.wikipedia.org
2 CONC /wiki/Hesse-Cassel '''Hesse-Cassel'''], a daughter of [https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Prince_William_of_Hesse-Kassel '''Prince William of Hesse-Kassel'''] and [https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Princess_Charlotte_of_Denmark '''Princess
2 CONC  Charlotte of Denmark''']. She spent most of her life in Denmark.
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT ===Family===
2 CONT
2 CONT '''Princess Augusta''' was born in Copenhagen as the youngest child of Prince William of Hesse, a son of [https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Prince_Frederick_of_Hesse-Kassel '''Prince Frederick of Hesse-Kassel'''] and [https://en.wikip
2 CONC edia.org/wiki/Princess_Caroline_of_Nassau-Usingen '''Princess Caroline of Nassau-Usingen'''] and Princess Charlotte of Denmark, a daughter of Hereditary Prince Frederick of Denmark and Norway (1753-1805) and Duchess Sophia Frederi
2 CONC ca of Mecklenburg-Schwerin (1758–1794). She was thus a niece of king Christian VIII of Denmark. Her sister was [https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Louise_of_Hesse-Kassel '''Louise of Hesse-Kassel'''], later Queen of Denmark and mother 
2 CONC to [https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Frederick_VIII_of_Denmark '''King Frederick VIII of Denmark'''], [https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Alexandra_of_Denmark '''Queen Alexandra'''] of The United Kingdom, [https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Ge
2 CONC orge_I_of_Greece King '''George I of Greece'''] and [https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Maria_Feodorovna_(Dagmar_of_Denmark%29 '''Empress Maria Feodorovna'''] of Russia.
2 CONT
2 CONT '''Her other siblings''' included her oldest sister [https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Princess_Marie_Luise_Charlotte_of_Hesse-Kassel '''Princess Marie Luise Charlotte of Hesse-Kassel'''] and her only brother [https://en.wikipedia.org
2 CONC /wiki/Prince_Frederick_William_of_Hesse-Kassel '''Prince Frederick William of Hesse-Kassel'''] (1820-1884), Head of the House of Hesse-Kassel after the death of the last elector of Hesse-Kassel, [https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Fred
2 CONC erick_William,_Elector_of_Hesse '''Frederick William, Elector of Hesse'''], who died without any legitimate issue.
2 CONT
2 CONT '''Augustas father''', Prince William, who was a minor prince of Hesse-Cassel, had moved to Denmark prior to his marriage to Princess Charlotte and Augusta and her siblings grew up in the Danish royal court and the family became o
2 CONC ne of the leading families in Danish society. The family became even more important when it became clear that the main line of the Danish royal house faced extinction. Augusta and her siblings were among the closest relatives of K
2 CONC ing Christian VIII and thus they had a strong claim to the throne. Due to various circumstances it was Augusta's brother-in-law, [https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Christian_IX_of_Denmark '''Christian IX of Denmark'''], who in the end
2 CONC  became king when the main line died out in 1863.
2 CONT
2 CONT ===Marriage===
2 CONT
2 CONT '''Princess Augusta''' married the Danish politician and Danish-Swedish nobleman, [https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Carl_Frederik_Blixen-Finecke '''Carl Frederik Blixen-Finecke'''], baron Blixen-Finecke in 1854. He held the family se
2 CONC at at Näsbyholm Castle in Sweden and Dallund manor in Funen and served as Danish Minister of Foreign Affairs in 1859-1860. The marriage produced two sons. The marriage was regarded with great distress in Augusta's family because C
2 CONC arl was married with two children when they fell in love and he divorced his wife to marry Augusta. He was furthermore of much lower rank than Augusta and later his political views were far from the views of her family. He also be
2 CONC came a close ally of [https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Louise_Rasmussen '''Countess Louise of Danner'''], the morganatic spouse of [https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Frederick_VII_of_Denmark King '''Frederick VII of Denmark'''], who was 
2 CONC disliked by the other members of the Danish royal family. Augusta and Carl had a very happy marriage despite the obstacles and they were known for their hospitality and lavish lifestyle. As a tribute to Augusta, Carl took the mott
2 CONC o "Per Angusta ad Augusta," which is latin for "through difficulties to honors." 
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT ===Last years===
2 CONT
2 CONT '''Princess Augusta''' became a widow in 1873. She lived for many years in "Villa Augusta" in the town of Helsingør north of Copenhagen. She lived privately at the villa, but she was often visited by the royal family, including em
2 CONC peror [https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Alexander_III_of_Russia '''Alexander III of Russia'''], when they stayed at Fredensborg Palace. She died at the [https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Amalienborg_Palace Amalienborg Palace] in 1889.
2 CONT
2 CONT Vigd 1 juni 1854
2 CONT
2 CONT Begraven i Skamby, Fyn
2 CONT
