1 NOTE {geni:about_me} ==Links:==
2 CONT *[http://thepeerage.com/p10573.htm#i105729 The Peerage] 
2 CONT *[http://www.geneall.net/W/per_page.php?id=9830 Geneall] 
2 CONT *[http://www.hansdenyngre.dk/hans_uk/wizg23.htm#1116 Johann the Younger #814]
2 CONT *[http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Grand_Duke_Michael_Pavlovich_of_Russia Wikipedia] 
2 CONT * Grand Duke Michael Pavlovich of Russia (Russian: Михаи́л Па́влович; Mikhail Pavlovich) (St. Petersburg, 8 February 1798 – Warsaw, 9 September 1849) was the tenth child and fourth son of Paul I of Russia and Sophie Dorothea of Wü
2 CONC rttemberg.
2 CONT
2 CONT ===Marriage and issue===
2 CONT * In St. Petersburg on 19 February 1824, Michael '''married''' his first cousin once removed Princess Charlotte of Württemberg (1807–1873), the daughter of Prince Paul of Württemberg and Charlotte of Saxe-Hildburghausen. Charlotte
2 CONC  took the name Elena Pavlovna upon converting to Orthodoxy. 
2 CONT * They had children
2 CONT ># Grand Duchess Maria Mikhailovna of Russia (9 March 1825 Moscow – 19 November 1846 Vienna); died unmarried.
2 CONT ># Grand Duchess Elizabeta Mikhailovna of Russia (26 May 1826 Moscow – 28 January 1845 Wiesbaden); married Adolf, Duke of Nassau and died in childbirth.
2 CONT ># Grand Duchess Ekaterina Mikhailovna of Russia (28 August 1827 – 12 May 1894), married Duke Georg August of Mecklenburg-Strelitz
2 CONT ># Grand Duke George Mikhailovich of Russia (16 September 1829 Moscow – 3 February 1890 Warsaw)
2 CONT ># Grand Duchess Alexandra Mikhailovna of Russia (28 January 1831 Moscow – 27 March 1832 Moscow)
2 CONT >#  Grand Duchess Anna Mikhailovna of Russia (27 October 1834 Moscow – 22 March 1836 Saint Petersburg)
2 CONT * Mikhailovsky Palace was built by Carlo Rossi for Grand Duke Michael between 1819–1825. The Palace now holds the Russian Museum.
2 CONT * Michael's great-great-great-grandson Duke Georg Borwin of Mecklenburg is the current head of the House of Mecklenburg-Strelitz.
2 CONT
2 CONT --------------------
2 CONT === GEDCOM Note ===
