1 NOTE {geni:about_me} '''From [https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/William_Hay,_19th_Earl_of_Erroll Wikipedia: William Hay, 19th Earl of Erroll]'''
2 CONT
2 CONT William Harry Hay, 19th Earl of Erroll (Saturday, 3 May 1823 – Thursday, 3 December 1891), styled Lord Hay between 1823 and 1831, and Lord Kilmarnock from 1831 to 1846, was a Scottish peer.
2 CONT
2 CONT ''Early life''
2 CONT
2 CONT William Harry Hay was born on Saturday, 3 May 1823. He was the only son of four children born to Lady Elizabeth FitzClarence and William Hay, 18th Earl of Erroll. His elder sister, Lady Ida Hay, married Charles Noel, 2nd Earl of G
2 CONC ainsborough (her descendants include the Earls of Gainsborough, the Marquesses of Bute and the Baronets of Bellingham). His younger sisters were Lady Agnes Hay, wife of James Duff, 5th Earl Fife (her son, Alexander Duff, 1st Duke 
2 CONC of Fife, married Princess Louise, daughter of King Edward VII), and Lady Alice Hay, who married Charles Edward Louis Casimir Stuart, Count d'Albanie (nephew of fraud John Sobieski Stuart).
2 CONT
2 CONT His paternal grandparents were William Hay, 17th Earl of Erroll and, his second wife, the former Alicia Eliot (third daughter of Samuel Eliot of Antigua). His mother was the illegitimate daughter of King William IV by his mistress
2 CONC , the famous comic actress Dora Bland (who was known as "Mrs. Jordan"). His maternal aunts and uncles were George FitzClarence, 1st Earl of Munster, Henry FitzClarence, Sophia FitzClarence (wife of Philip Sidney, 1st Baron De L'Is
2 CONC le and Dudley), Mary FitzClarence (wife of Charles Richard Fox), Lord Frederick FitzClarence, Lord Adolphus FitzClarence, Augusta FitzClarence, Lord Augustus FitzClarence, and Amelia FitzClarence (wife of Lucius Cary, 10th Viscoun
2 CONC t Falkland).
2 CONT
2 CONT ''Career''
2 CONT
2 CONT Lord Erroll served as the third Page of Honour from 1832 to 1839 (for his grandfather, King William IV, from 1832 to 1837, and for Queen Victoria, his grandfather's niece, from 1837 to 1839).
2 CONT
2 CONT From 1841 to 1860, he served in the British Army.
2 CONT
2 CONT ''Personal life''
2 CONT
2 CONT On Wednesday, 20 September 1848, he was married to Eliza Amelia Gore (1829–1916), the eldest daughter of Gen. Hon. Sir Charles Stephen Gore (the third son, by his second wife, of Arthur Gore, 2nd Earl of Arran) and the former Sara
2 CONC h Rachel Fraser (eldest daughter of James Fraser, a member of the Council of Nova Scotia).[a] The Countess of Erroll served as a Lady of the Bedchamber to Queen Alexandra (wife of King Edward VII) beginning in 1872. Together, they
2 CONC  were the parents of seven children:
2 CONT
2 CONT * Hon. Charles Gore Hay, Master of Erroll, styled Lord Kilmarnock (1850–1850), who died in infancy.
2 CONT * Charles Gore Hay, 20th Earl of Erroll (1852–1927), who married Mary Caroline L'Estrange, youngest daughter of Edmund L'Estrange of Tynte Lodge.
2 CONT * CaptainHon. Arthur Hay (1855–1932), who served in Egypt in 1882 and Burma in 1887 and was a Gentleman Usher from 1896 to 1925; he was awarded CVO.
2 CONT * Lady Florence Alice Hay (1858–1859), who died young.
2 CONT * Lady Cecilia Leila Hay (1860–1935), married CaptainGeorge Allan Webbe of Errollston (died Thursday, 19 February 1925), in 1883.
2 CONT * Hon. Francis Hay (1864–1898), a Page of Honour.
2 CONT * Lady Florence Agnes Adelaide Hay (1872–1935), who married Maj. Henry Wolrige-Gordon (died 1923) in 1895.
2 CONT
2 CONT Lord Erroll died on Thursday, 3 December 1891. His widow, the Dowager Countess of Erroll, died on Saturday, 11 March 1916.
2 CONT
2 CONT ''Descendants''
2 CONT
2 CONT Through his eldest surviving son Charles, he was a grandfather of Victor Alexander Sereld Hay, who died in 1928 a year after becoming the 21st Earl of Erroll.
2 CONT
2 CONT '''From [https://www.britishnewspaperarchive.com/image-share/09e2dd55-34c8-48d3-8fec-762c6d557b9d Derby Mercury Wednesday 7 May 1823 Page 3 Births]'''
2 CONT
2 CONT Births: On Saturday morning, 3 May 1823, at the house of his Royal Highness the Duke of Clarence, Bushy Park [https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Bushy_House Bushy House, Bushy Road, Teddington, London TW11 0EQ 51.42028, -0.33917], the 
2 CONC Countess of Erroll, of a son and heir.
2 CONT
2 CONT '''From [https://www.britishnewspaperarchive.com/image-share/28de5248-56ee-4f79-8448-c350408f9901 Globe Thursday, 3 December 1891 Page 3 Obituary]'''
2 CONT
2 CONT The Exchange Telegraph Company announces that the Earl of Erroll died today, Thursday, 3 December 1891, at [https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/New_Slains_Castle New Slains Castle, Cruden Bay, Aberdeenshire AB42 0NE 57.4153354, -1.83229
2 CONC 35].
2 CONT
2 CONT William Harry Hay, 18th Earl, was born on Saturday, 3 May 1823, and succeeded to the title in 1846. He was educated at Eton, was a major in the Rifle Brigade, and served in the Crimea, where he was wounded. Among other positions h
2 CONC e held, he was Hereditary Lord High Constable and Knight Marischal of Scotland. In 1848 the late Earl married Eliza Amelia Gore, daughter of the late General the Hon. Sir Charles Gore.
2 CONT
2 CONT Lord Kilmarnock succeeds to the title.
2 CONT
2 CONT '''From [https://www.findagrave.com/memorial/203927377/william-harry-hay findagrave: Major William Harry Hay (1823-1891)]'''
2 CONT
2 CONT * Name: William Harry Hay (Veteran)
2 CONT * Born: Saturday, 3 May 1823, London, England
2 CONT * Died: Thursday, 3 December 1891 (aged 68), Kirktown of Slains, Aberdeenshire, Scotland
2 CONT * Buried: [Cruden Graveyard, Hatton, Aberdeenshire AB42 0QB  57.41937, -1.88410], Scotland
2 CONT * Plot: [Plot 57.4192528, -1.8837389]
2 CONT * Inscription: (tidied)
2 CONT ** William Harry Hay
2 CONT ** Eighteenth Earl of Erroll
2 CONT ** Born Saturday, 3 May 1823
2 CONT ** Died Thursday, 3 December 1891
2 CONT * About: Manchester Courier and Lancashire General Advertiser - Saturday, 5 December 1891, page 20 Death of the Earl of Erroll. 
2 CONT
2 CONT The Earl of Errol died on Wednesday night 2 December 1891 at Slains Castle, Aberdeenshire. The deceased was the 18th earl, his mother being Lady Elizabeth Fitz-Clarence, natural daughter of King William IV. 
2 CONT
2 CONT He entered the Army in 1841, served in the Rifle Brigade until 1860, and was wounded at the battle of Alma. 
2 CONT
2 CONT He was hereditary Lord High Constable of Scotland, the highest hereditary distinction in the United Kingdom after those enjoyed by the Royal Family.
2 CONT
2 CONT His son, Lord Kilmarnock succeeds to the title.
2 CONT
2 CONT 18th Earl of Erroll although sometimes recorded as the 19th.
2 CONT
2 CONT '''From [https://www.myheritage.com/research/record-40001-320107202/william-harry-hay-19th-earl-of-erroll-in-familysearch-family-tree MyHeritage: William Harry Hay 19th Earl of Erroll: FamilySearch Family Tree]'''
2 CONT
2 CONT * name: William Harry Hay 19th Earl of Erroll
2 CONT * birth name: William Henry Hay
2 CONT * gender: Male
2 CONT * born: Saturday, 3 May 1823 at London, England
2 CONT * father: William George Hay 18th Earl of Erroll
2 CONT * siblings: Ida Harriet Augusta Noel Countess of Gainsborough (born Hay), Lady Agnes Georgiana Elizabeth Duff (born Hay), Alice Mary Emily Allen (born Hay)
2 CONT * marriage: Eliza Amelia Gore on Wednesday, 20 September 1848 at Montreal, Quebec, Canada
2 CONT * wife: Eliza Amelia Hay (born Gore)
2 CONT * children: Charles Gore Hay Lord Kilmarnock, Charles Gore Hay 20th Earl Of Erroll, Arthur Hay, Florence Alice Hay, Lady Cecilia Leila Webbe (born Hay), Francis Hay, Florence Agnes Adelaide Gordon (born Hay)
2 CONT * census: Sunday, 7 April 1861 at St George Hanover Square, London, England
2 CONT * census: Sunday, 3 April 1881 at Cruden, Aberdeenshire, Scotland
