2 CONT
2 CONT Frederick VIII (1843-1912), king of Denmark (1906-12), born in Copenhagen, 
2 CONT and educated at the University of Oxford. He succeeded to the throne on 
2 CONT the death of his father, Christian IX. His son, Prince Charles, became 
2 CONT Hakon VII, king of Norway, in 1905. Frederick was a brother of Alexandra 
2 CONT (1844-1925), queen consort of Great Britain, and of George I, king of 
2 CONT Greece.
