2 CONT *[http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Grand_Duke_Michael_Nikolaevich_of_Russia Wikipedia]
2 CONT --------------------
2 CONT Grand Duke Michael Nikolaevich of Russia (25 October 1832 – 18 December 1909) was the fourth son and seventh child of Tsar Nicholas I of Russia and Charlotte of Prussia. He was the first owner of the New Michael Palace on the Pala
2 CONC ce Quay in Saint Petersburg.
2 CONT
2 CONT On 16 August 1857, he married Princess Cecily Auguste of Baden (1839–1891), daughter of Leopold, Grand Duke of Baden and Sophie of Sweden. Cecily adopted the name Olga Fedorovna, and had 7 children. 
2 CONT
2 CONT He served 20 years (1862–1882) as the Governor General of Caucasia, being seated in Tbilisi, the town which most of his children remembered as the home of their childhood. In the course of his life, four members of his family rule
2 CONC d as Emperors of Russia: his father, Nicholas I; his brother, Alexander II; his nephew, Alexander III; as well as his grand-nephew, Nicholas II, whose second daughter, Grand Duchess Tatiana, the Grand Duke was godfather to. He die
2 CONC d in Cannes, France, on 18 December 1909. He was the last surviving legitimate grandchild of Paul I of Russia.
