1 OCCU Herzog v. Urach 1869-1928, King of Lithuania July 1918-November 1918, Army general, Royal Duke (Herzog), Dr. phil., Hertug/greve, General
1 NOTE {geni:about_me} Succeeded as 2nd Duke (Herzog) when a child. Wilhelm's main career was in the army, and in 1914 was general of the 26th division:
2 CONT
2 CONT http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/26th_Division_%28German_Empire%29
2 CONT
2 CONT He retired as a general in 1917 and now is most famous for being briefly elected King of Lithuania in 1918, styled "Mindaugas II":
2 CONT
2 CONT http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Mindaugas_II_of_Lithuania
2 CONT
2 CONT Spent much of his youth in Monaco with his mother, until her death in 1897. He was the legitimate heir to Monaco until the changes effected in 1911-18:
2 CONT
2 CONT http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Monaco_Succession_Crisis_of_1918
2 CONT
