1 NOTE He was called Frederick the Fair, Habsburg king of Germany and Prussia.  
2 CONT Frederick became duke of Austria in 1306 and was elected king of Germany 
2 CONT by a minority of electors in 1314; the majority favored Louis IV, duke of 
2 CONT Bavaria. After eight years of conflict, Louis defeated and imprisoned 
2 CONT (1322) Frederick, but later released (1325) him and recognized him as 
2 CONT coruler. His authority, however, was limited to Austria.
1 NOTE KING OF PRUSSIA; EMPORER OF GERMANY; KG; HAD 6 OTHER CHILDREN BESIDES THOSE
2 CONT LISTED
