2 CONT *[http://www.hansdenyngre.dk/hans_uk/wizg27.htm#773 Johann the Younger #1386] + [http://hansdenyngre.dk/hans_uk/wizg32.htm#774 # 1609]
2 CONT *[http://de.wikipedia.org/wiki/Maria_Anna_von_Preu%C3%9Fen Deutsch]
2 CONT
2 CONT https://www.findagrave.com/memorial/36126645/maria_anna_friederike-von_preussen
2 CONT
2 CONT Princess Maria Anna Friederike of Prussia. German royalty.
2 CONT
2 CONT Anna was the youngest of the three children of Prince Charles of Prussia and Princess Marie of Saxe-Weimar. On May 26, 1853, Anna married Prince Frederick William of Hesse-Cassel at Charlottenburg Palace in Berlin. Anna was the se
2 CONC cond wife of her new husband, who nine years previously had experienced the traumatic death in childbirth of his beloved first wife, Alexandra Nikolaevna of Russia. Anna died in Frankfurt at the age of 82. She is buried in the cat
2 CONC hedral at Fulda in front of the altar to St. Anne.
2 CONT Inscription
2 CONT Hic jacet Serenissima Landgravia Hessiae
2 CONT ANNA
2 CONT Principissa Borussiae
2 CONT nata Berolini die 17 Maii 1836
2 CONT obiit Francofurti die 12 Iunii 1918
2 CONT Misericordias Domini in aeternum cantabo.
2 CONT R.I.P.
2 CONT
2 CONT In English:
2 CONT Here lies the most serene Landgravine of Hesse
2 CONT ANNA
2 CONT Princess of Prussia
2 CONT Born in Berlin, 17 May 1836
2 CONT Died in Frankfurt, 12 June 1918
2 CONT I will sing the mercies of the Lord forever.
2 CONT R.I.P.
