1 NOTE {geni:about_me} 1912 ~ 2003
2 CONT    Velda Haslam Johnson, 90, Provo, passed away May 17, 2003.
2 CONT    She was born Dec 5, 1912 in American Fork, UT the youngest of 13 children of Joshua and Alice Haslam. She attended public schools in Bennet and Vernal. She graduated from Vernal High School.
2 CONT    Velda married Carl Edwin Johnson Aug 8, 1936. The marriage was later solemnized in the Salt Lake LDS Temple. A son, Carl Mauritz Johnson, was born to them Feb 22, 1939.
2 CONT    With the outbreak of World War II, her husband, Carl, was called to active duty with the army Jan 26, 1942. Upon his departure for the South Pacific she received training as a bank teller and went to work for Walker Bank in Sal
2 CONC t Lake City. After Carl returned home from the service they moved briefly to Vernal and then to Berkeley, CA where Carl had been accepted to the University of California. In Berkeley Velda worked several years at banks in the area
2 CONC  and then accepted a position in the Cashier's Office at the University of California. She remained at the university until she retired. She then opened her own interior decorating business until Carl retired and they returned to 
2 CONC Utah.
2 CONT    Upon their retirement they built a home in Orem. They worked as ordinance workers in the Provo Temple for three years and then served an LDS mission in the Florida Tampa Mission. Following their mission they bought a home on Gr
2 CONC andview Hill, Provo to be closer to their son, his wife, and their grandchildren.
2 CONT    After Velda suffered a stroke in 1996, she and Carl moved to the Seville Retirement Center, Orem and then later to Courtyard at Jamestown, Provo. Carl died Feb 24, 2003.
2 CONT    Velda has now moved to the other side of the veil to join Carl and have glorious reunions with her parents, brothers, sisters and friends. She is survived by her son, Carl (Els-Britt), three grandchildren and one great-grandchi
2 CONC ld. She was dearly loved by all who knew her and will be deeply missed.
2 CONT    Services, under the direction of Walker Sanderson Funeral Home, Or-em, will be Wed. May 21, 2 p.m. Grandview South LDS Stake Center, 1122 N. Grand Ave, Provo. Friends may call 12:45-1:45 p.m. prior to the services. Burial, Amer
2 CONC ican Fork City Cemetery. (Obituary printed in the Deseret News May 19, 2003)
