1 NOTE {geni:about_me} Paternal Haplogroup
2 CONT
2 CONT R-S22047
2 CONT
2 CONT HEART ATTACK CLAIMS LIFE OF JOHN H. HASLEM
2 CONT
2 CONT Funeral services were held Saturday, January 21, in memory of John Henry Haslem, in the Olpin Mortuary in Pleasant Grove, under the direction of Bishop Frede E. Thomsen of the Salt Lake City Tenth LDS Ward.
2 CONT
2 CONT The family prayer was given by Myron B. Haslem. Prelude and postlude music was palyed by Kay H. Watt. A musical number was given by Norman R. Haslem and Nila H. Batty, accompanied by Joyleen B. Haslem. The invocation was presented
2 CONC  by Acel Haslem. Sue Zann W. Kohler presented a philosophy of life, followed by a musical number given by the small great-grandchildren, directed by Flossie H. Walker. Dean W. Haslem was the next speaker, followed by another music
2 CONC al number by Don Haslem on the organ. The final speaker was Lynn Haslem followed by Bishop Frede E. Thomsen who offered remarks, and a final musical number by N. Chad Watt, accompanied by Kay H. Watt. The benediction was given by 
2 CONC Verl Haslem. The dedication of the grave in the American Fork Cemetery was by Kenneth J. Haslem.
2 CONT
2 CONT Pallbearers were Malcolm J. McLeod, Melvin J. McLeod, Max Haslem, Kenneth J. Haslem, Edwin S. Lewis and Wendell G. Russon.
2 CONT
2 CONT John Henry Haslem, 87, Salt Lake, died January 21, at a son's home in Beaver of a heart ailment. He was born August 11, 1888 in Vernal to Joshua and Alice Southam Haslem. He married Florence Wagstaff January 15, 1908, in the Salt 
2 CONC Lake LDS Temple. She died October 30, 1918. He married Rebecca Hartle, June 1, 1923, in the Salt Lake LDS Temple. She died March 2, 1965. He married Pearl McLeod, June 6, 1966, in Salt Lake City. He was a retired farmer of the Uin
2 CONC tah Basin. 
2 CONT
2 CONT Survivors: wife, sons, daughters, Kenneth, Salt Lake City; Niles, Vernal; Mrs. Arvil (Helen) Wadley, Pleasant Grove; Dena, Logan; Mrs. Edwin (Rhea) Lewis, Mrs. Wendell (Marie) Russon, Acel, all of Orem; Lynn, Beaver; Verl, Myron, 
2 CONC Roosevelt; 58 grandchildren, 69 great-grandchildren, 2 great-great-grandchildren, brothers, sisters, Clair, Orem; Von Roosevelt; Ruth Anderson, Reno, Nevada; Gladys Price; Katie Horrocks, both of Vernal; Mrs. Lloyd (Florence) Brow
2 CONC n, Salt Lake; Velda Johnson, California; step-sons and step-daughters, Malcolm McLeod, Salt Lake City; Melvin McLeod, Mrs. Roy (Donn) Ipson, both of Bountiful; Mrs. Richard (Marjorie) Smith, Roy; Mrs. Howard (Betty) Russell, Murra
2 CONC y.
2 CONT
2 CONT -Vernal Express, Obituaries, February 5, 1976, transcribed by Rhonda Holton
