1 NOTE {geni:about_me} '''From [https://www.britishnewspaperarchive.co.uk/viewer/bl/0002751/18720607/059/0005 British Newspaper Archive: Montrose Standard Friday, 7 June 1872 Page 5 Births]'''
2 CONT
2 CONT Births: At [https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/New_Slains_Castle New Slains Castle, Cruden Bay, Aberdeenshire AB42 0NE 57.4153354, -1.8322935], on Friday, 31 May 1872 [ult.], the Countess of Errol, of a daughter.
2 CONT
2 CONT '''From [https://www.freebmd.org.uk/cgi/information.pl?cite=JqF3xOA0vKB60CfLwYIbvw&scan=1 FreeBMD: Registration of marriage of Florence Agnes A. Hay in 1895] and [https://www.freebmd.org.uk/cgi/information.pl?cite=cBknl3vBIjNRo2rH
2 CONC xAfsUg&scan=1 FreeBMD: Registration of marriage of Henry Gordon W. Gordon in 1895]'''
2 CONT
2 CONT * April to June 1895: Registration of marriage of Henry Gordon W. Gordon; in Chelsea (Volume 1a, Page 744)
2 CONT * April to June 1895: Registration of marriage of Florence Agnes A. Hay; in Chelsea (Volume 1a, Page 744)
2 CONT
2 CONT '''From [https://www.britishnewspaperarchive.co.uk/viewer/bl/0000693/18950518/082/0012 British Newspaper Archive: Penny Illustrated Paper Saturday, 18 May 1895 Page 12 The World of Women: Marriage of Lady Florence Hay and Captain 
2 CONC H. Wolrige Gordon]'''
2 CONT
2 CONT The Presbyterian Church of [https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/St_Columba%27s_Church,_London St Columba's Church, Pont Street, London SW1X 0BD 51.496778, -0.16333], was the scene of a brilliant ceremony on Thursday, 9 May 1895 when Cap
2 CONC tain Harry Wolrige Gordon led the Lady Florence Hay to the altar. 
2 CONT
2 CONT The gallant bridegroom is a Captain in the 79th Cameron Highlanders, and has seen a good deal of active service, being engaged in the Nile Campaign and present at the Battle of Ghinness, where he received his medal and Khedive's s
2 CONC tar. 
2 CONT
2 CONT He is the youngest son of Mr. Henry Wolrige Gordon, J.P. and D.L. for Aberdeenshire, of [Esslemont House and Garden, Ellon, Aberdeenshire AB41 8PA 57.35694, -2.11722] and [https://britishlistedbuildings.co.uk/200341477-mains-of-ha
2 CONC llhead-leochel-cushnie Mains of Hallhead, Leochel-Cushnie, Aberdeenshire AB33 8LR 57.1705, -2.7872], and [53 Queen's Gate, South Kensington, London SW7 5JW 51.4964088, -0.1796919]. 
2 CONT
2 CONT ''The Charming Bride.''
2 CONT
2 CONT Lady Florence Agnes Adelaide Hay, youngest daughter of the Dowager Countess of Enroll (a lady-in-waiting to H.M. the Queen), sister to the present Earl of Erroll, and related by marriage to the well-known cricketer, Mr. A. J. Webb
2 CONC e, is a general favourite in all classes of society, having specially endeared herself to the people of Port Erroll, N.B., by her kindness, affability, and warm interest in the welfare of all. 
2 CONT
2 CONT The bride was attended by four bridesmaids — Miss Gordon, Miss Mary Gore, Miss Margaret Orde, and Miss Sinclair. They wore dresses of fawn-coloured createdépon, with neck-bands and coloured silk fronts of different hues, their lar
2 CONC ge hats being of white chip ornamented with varied roses. 
2 CONT
2 CONT The Earl of Erroll gave his sister away. She had selected a gown of white satin, lined with pink silk and trimmed with Maltese lace, her full Court train being also lined with the same beautiful shade of pale pink. A fine tulle ve
2 CONC il and some superb diamonds completed a much-admired bridal costume. 
2 CONT
2 CONT Captain Walter Gordon Wolrige Gordon, of the Black Watch (a brother of the bridegroom), was best man. 
2 CONT
2 CONT Among the distinguished company present in the church were H.R.H. the Duchess of Fife and the Duke of Fife. 
2 CONT
2 CONT After the reception, held at [9 Queen's Gate Terrace, South Kensington, London SW7 5PE 51.4985408, -0.1807364], Captain Harry and Lady Florence Wolridge Gordon left for Esslemont, North Britain [N.B.], where they will spend the Ho
2 CONC neymoon. 
2 CONT
2 CONT The presents were of a most beautiful and costly description. Her Majesty the Queen gave a diamond brooch; Princess Beatrice, a large silver-framed mirror; the Marchioness of Lorne, a pair of vases; the Duke and Duchess of Fife, a
2 CONC  white ostrich-feather fan; and the Duke and Duchess of Teck, a ruby, diamond, and pearl brooch, etc.
2 CONT
2 CONT '''From [https://www.myheritage.com/research/record-10446-5373809/eliza-amelia-erroll-in-1911-england-wales-census MyHeritage: Eliza Amelia Erroll: 1911 England & Wales Census]'''
2 CONT
2 CONT 2 April 1911 Census for residents of [https://maps.nls.uk/geo/explore/#zoom=17.8&lat=51.48418&lon=-0.28956&layers=168&b=1&o=100&marker=51.483952,-0.290472 Kew Cottage, 51 Kew Green, Kew, London TW9 3AA 51.483952, -0.290472], Engla
2 CONC nd; House with 17 rooms
2 CONT * Eliza Amelia Erroll, head, widow [married 63 years ago [about 1848], 7 children, 5 still living], female, aged 82 [born about 1829], in Quebec, Canada; Occupation: Private Means
2 CONT * Florence Wolrige Gordon, visitor, married for 16 years [about 1895], no children, female, aged 38 [born about 1873], in Cruden, Aberdeenshire; Occupation: Private Means
2 CONT * 1 other visitor, 4 servants
2 CONT
2 CONT '''From [https://www.freebmd.org.uk/cgi/information.pl?cite=KzMpT68NV22A9HROaocyqQ&scan=1 FreeBMD: Registration of death of Florence A. A. W. Gordon in 1935]'''
2 CONT
2 CONT October to December 1935: Registration of death of Florence A. A. W. Gordon; aged 63 [born about 1872]; in Radnorshire West (Volume 11b, Page 141)
2 CONT
2 CONT '''From [https://www.britishnewspaperarchive.co.uk/viewer/bl/0000540/19351017/066/0011 British Newspaper Archive: The Scotsman Thursday, 17 October 1935 Page 11 Death of Lady Florence Gordon, great-aunt of the present Earl of Erro
2 CONC ll]'''
2 CONT
2 CONT Lady Florence Gordon, widow of Major H. Wolrige Gordon, died last night Wednesday, 16 October 1935, at Llandrindod Wells, aged 63. She was the great-aunt of the present Earl of Erroll. She took a great interest in local affairs, a
2 CONC nd had been president of the women's golf club, the Development Association, and the women's bowling club. She had also held offices in the Radnorshire and Llandrindod Wells Women's Unionist Associations.
2 CONT
2 CONT '''From [https://www.findagrave.com/memorial/205815180/florence-agnes_adelaide_hay-gordon findagrave: Florence Agnes Adelaide Hay Gordon (1872-1935)]'''
2 CONT
2 CONT * Name: Florence Agnes Adelaide Gordon (née Hay)
2 CONT * Born: Sunday, 31 March 1872
2 CONT * Died: Wednesday, 16 October 1935 (aged 63)
2 CONT * Buried: [Llandrindod Wells Cemetery, Ithon Road, Llandrindod Wells, Powys, Wales LD1 6BY 52.25010, -3.38562]
2 CONT * Inscription:
2 CONT ** In memory of Henry Gordon Wolrige Gordon, Major, 79th Cameron Highlanders,
2 CONT ** born Wednesday, 14 January 1863, died Tuesday, 9 October 1923.
2 CONT ** Also of Florence Agnes Adelaide Hay,
2 CONT ** daughter of William [Hay], 19th Earl of Erroll, hereditary Lord High Constable of Scotland,
2 CONT ** and wife of Major H. G. Wolrige Gordon,
2 CONT ** born Friday, 31 May 1872, died Wednesday, 16 October 1935
2 CONT
2 CONT '''From [https://www.myheritage.com/research/record-10691-5640203/lady-florence-agnes-adelaide-hay-wolrige-gordon-check-in-england-wales-index-of-wills-probates MyHeritage: Probate index 1936]'''
2 CONT
2 CONT 1 July 1936 probate of Lady Florence Agnes Adelaide Hay or Wolrige Gordon of [Sunnycroft, Princes Avenue, Llandrindod Wells, Radnorshire, Wales LD1 5HU 52.238502, -3.3768368], who died Wednesday, 16 October 1935, at [The Wingfield
2 CONC  Nursing Home, location?], Llandrindod Wells, probate granted (confirmation) at London on 1 July 1936 to John Reid Dean and Charles Grant Brown, advocates.
2 CONT
