1 NOTE {geni:about_me} '''From [https://www.freebmd.org.uk/cgi/information.pl?cite=G9wjVoVaVqW2UUrlMipUcA&scan=1 FreeBMD: Registration of marriage of Dora Mina E. Wemyss in 1887] and [https://www.freebmd.org.uk/cgi/information.pl?cite=CG
2 CONC LufciV0k6wXYJKXX2OKg&scan=1 FreeBMD: Registration of marriage of Henry George Grosvenor in 1887]'''
2 CONT
2 CONT * April to June 1887: Registration of marriage of Henry George Grosvenor; in Kensington (Volume 1a, Page 321)
2 CONT * April to June 1887: Registration of marriage of Dora Mina E. Wemyss; in Kensington (Volume 1a, Page 321)
2 CONT
2 CONT '''From [https://www.myheritage.com/research/record-10155-16468201/lord-henery-g-grosvenor-in-1891-england-wales-census MyHeritage: Lord Henry G Grosvenor: 1891 England & Wales Census]'''
2 CONT
2 CONT 5 April 1891 Census for residents of [https://britishlistedbuildings.co.uk/101073846-the-cottage-ketton The Cottage, Aldgate, Ketton, Rutland PE9 3TD 52.6282, -0.5482], England
2 CONT * Lord Henry G Grosvenor, head, married, male, aged 29 [born about 1862], in North Kensington, London; Occupation: Living on own means
2 CONT * Dora Grosvenor, wife, married, female, aged 34 [born about 1857], in Fife, Scotland
2 CONT * Millicent Grosvenor, daughter, single, female, aged 2 [born about 1889], in Mayfair, London
2 CONT * Dorothy Grosvenor, daughter, single, female, aged 7 months, [born about August 1890], in Stamford, Northamptonshire
2 CONT * Joseph Fenton, servant, single, male, aged 30 [born about 1861], in Weston, Staffordshire; Occupation: Butler Domestic
2 CONT * Patrick Delaney, servant, single, male, aged 29 [born about 1862], in Liverpool, Lancashire; Occupation: Groom Domestic
2 CONT * James Morgan, servant, single, male, aged 22 [born about 1869], in Cameron, Scotland; Occupation: Groom Domestic
2 CONT * William Cornell, servant, single, male, aged 18 [born about 1873], in Ashby, Leicestershire; Occupation: Groom Domestic
2 CONT * William Arthur, servant, single, male, aged 17 [born about 1874], in St George's, London; Occupation: Footman Domestic
2 CONT * Mary Dynian[?], servant, single, female, aged 45 [born about 1846], in Cantaff[?], Ireland; Occupation: Housekeeper Domestic
2 CONT * Isabella Rogers, servant, single, female, aged 57 [born about 1834], in Montrose, Scotland; Occupation: Nurse Domestic
2 CONT * Mary Cook, servant, single, female, aged 24 [born about 1867], in Cranborne, Dorset; Occupation: Kitchenmaid Domestic
2 CONT * Louisa Rayson[?], servant, single, female, aged 36 [born about 1855], in Oxton, Nottinghamshire; Occupation: Housemaid Domestic
2 CONT * Helena Bishop, servant, single, female, aged 21 [born about 1870], in Moorhouse, Kent; Occupation: Nursemaid Domestic
2 CONT * Janet Cunningham, servant, single, female, aged 22 [born about 1869], in Balgurair[?], Scotland; Occupation: Housemaid Domestic
2 CONT * Jane Quincey[?], servant, single, female, aged 21 [born about 1870], in Braceborough, Lincolnshire; Occupation: Scullery Maid Domestic
2 CONT
2 CONT '''From [https://www.freebmd.org.uk/cgi/information.pl?cite=04N94cMY%2FiVu40uupn4OXg&scan=1 FreeBMD: Registration of death of Dora Nina K. Grosvenor in 1894]'''
2 CONT
2 CONT October to December 1894: Registration of death of Dora Nina K. Grosvenor; aged 38 [born about 1856]; in Chester (Volume 8a, Page 253)
2 CONT
2 CONT '''From [https://www.britishnewspaperarchive.co.uk/viewer/bl/0000275/18941226/006/0003 British Newspaper Archive: Sheffield Evening Telegraph Wednesday, 26 December 1894 Page 3 Death of Lady Henry Grosvenor]'''
2 CONT
2 CONT ''Sad Affair at Eaton Hall''
2 CONT
2 CONT A Chester correspondent telegraphed last night, Tuesday, 25 December 1894: — Deep gloom overspread Chester and Cheshire this morning, on receipt of the news of the death of Lady Henry Grosvenor, daughter-in-Law of the Duke of West
2 CONC minster, at Eaton Hall. Her ladyship, who had recently been in delicate health, was seized suddenly on Saturday week, 15 December 1894 with cerebral symptoms, due to uraemia. Last Sunday night, 23 December 1894, she was delivered 
2 CONC of a son, and subsequently her condition caused the gravest anxiety to the family and her medical attendants — Dr. Champneys, her London physician, Dr. Dobie, and Dr. Herry Dobie, of Chester. Early on Monday, 24 December 1894, the
2 CONC  patient's condition became critical, and the frequent bulletins
2 CONT
2 CONT ''assumed a more hopeless form.''
2 CONT
2 CONT She retained consciousness more or less, and rallied late in the evening, but sank rapidly, and expired ten minutes before midnight on Christmas Eve. The infant son is still alive, and was baptised on Monday, 24 December 1894.
2 CONT
2 CONT The deceased, Lady Dora Mina Erskine Wemyss, came of a distinguished old Scottish family, being the eldest daughter of the late James Hay Erskine Wemyss, of Wemyss Castle and Torrie House, Fifeshire, Lord Lieutenant and M.P. for F
2 CONC ifeshire. She married, in 1887, Lord Henry Grosvenor, third son of the Duke of Westminster, and leaves, besides the infant son, two daughters, the elder of whom, Miss Millicent Constance, who will be five years old next month, was
2 CONC  bridesmaid at the wedding of Lady Margaret Grosvenor and Prince Adolphus of Teck a fortnight ago. Lady Henry was also
2 CONT
2 CONT ''a guest at the wedding.''
2 CONT
2 CONT The deceased's mother, sister, and brothers had been summoned to Eaton when the gravity of the case had been realised, and they were present at the deathbed, along with the Duke and Duchess of Westminster, Lord Henry Grosvenor, th
2 CONC e Marchioness of Ormonde, the Countess Grosvenor, Lady Chesham, and nearly all the rest of the family. Prince and Princess Adolphus of Teck arrived on Saturday evening, but had to leave for White Lodge, Richmond, on Monday afterno
2 CONC on.
2 CONT
2 CONT A telegram from Eaton Hall last night stated that the funeral of Lady Henry Grosvenor will take place tomorrow, Thursday, 27 December 1894, at noon, at Eccleston Church, near Eaton Hall.
2 CONT
2 CONT '''From [https://www.findagrave.com/memorial/203338815/dora_mina_kittina_grosvenor findagrave: Dora Mina Kittina Grosvenor (née Erskine-Wemyss) (1856-1894)]'''
2 CONT
2 CONT * Name: Dora Mina Kittina Grosvenor (née Erskine-Wemyss)
2 CONT * Born: Wednesday, 6 February 1856, Fife, Scotland
2 CONT * Died: Tuesday, 25 December 1894 (aged 38), Eaton (Chester), Cheshire West and Chester, Cheshire, England
2 CONT * Buried: [St Mary the Virgin Churchyard, Church Road, Eccleston, Cheshire CH4 9HT 53.15701, -2.87926], England
2 CONT * Plot: [Plot 53.1581188, -2.8791833]
2 CONT * About:
2 CONT
2 CONT Dora Mina Kittina Erskine-Wemyss was born at Wemyss Castle, Fife, Scotland on Wednesday, 6 February 1856. Her parents were James Hay Erskine-Wemyss (1829-1864) and Millicent Ann Mary Kennedy-Erskine (1831-1895), a granddaughter of
2 CONC  King  William IV (1765-1837) and Dorothea Bland (1761-1816).
2 CONT
2 CONT Dora Erskine-Wemyss had a strong social conscience. In 1877, aged 21 years, she established the Wemyss School of Needlework in Coaltown of Wemyss, the closest village to Wemyss Castle. Dora, inspired by the opening of the Royal Sc
2 CONC hool of Needlework in London five years earlier, sought to offer young women six-month apprenticeships. If they showed talent they stayed on as employees of the school, found work as ladies’ maids or worked in their own homes.
2 CONT
2 CONT Dora married Lord Henry George Grosvenor (1861-1914), a younger son of, 1 st Duke of Westminster (1825-99), at St Peter, Cranley Gardens, Kensington on Thursday, 21 April 1887. Lord and Lady Henry Grosvenor divided their time betw
2 CONC een Bulwich Park, Wansford, Northamptonshire and Grosvenor properties in Cheshire and London. Three children were born to the couple:
2 CONT
2 CONT # Millicent Constance (1889-1944).
2 CONT # Dorothy Alice Margaret Augusta (1890-1966).
2 CONT # William, 3rd Duke of Westminster (1894-1963).
2 CONT
2 CONT Whilst at [https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Eaton_Hall,_Cheshire Eaton Hall, Belgrave Avenue, Belgrave, Cheshire CH4 9JF 53.1403, -2.8775], Dora’s baby son was born at six months gestation on Sunday, 23 December 1894. Not expected to
2 CONC  thrive, the baby was baptised the following day. Dora, much weakened by his birth, died as Christmas Eve passed into Christmas Day.
