2 TITL  Открытка из Царского Села 13 Января 1905 года.
1 NOTE OR "ALICKY"; ON HER MARRIAGE BECAME "ALEXANDRA FEODOROVNA"; EXECUTED
1 NOTE Alexandra was the daughter of the Grand Duke of Hesse-Darmstadt, born 6 June 1872, and was also the grand daughter of Queen Victoria of England.
2 CONT
2 CONT After the RUSSIAN REVOLUTION of 1917, Alexandra and Nicholas and all their children were shot on the night of July 16-17 in Ekaterinburg (now Sverdiovsk) Russia.  Their bodies were hidden in a secret mass grave only recently re-di
2 CONC scovered.
2 CONT
2 CONT Alexandra Fyodorovna, Empress of Russia, became a determined, narrow-minded reactionary, with pretensions to mysticism, and she dominated her irresolute husband, Tsar Nicholas.  During World War I she became the virtual ruler of r
2 CONC ussia, and the debauched monk Grigory Yefimovich RASPUTIN who claimed healing powers, was her chief advisor. (Anthony Bird Bibliography; Massie, Robert K. for Grolier's).
