1 NOTE {geni:about_me} '''Prince Maurice Victor Donald of Battenberg, KCVO''' (3 October 1891 – 27 October 1914)
2 CONT
2 CONT Prince Maurice of Battenberg, KCVO, was a member of the Hessian princely Battenberg family and the extended British Royal Family, a grandson of Queen Victoria and her youngest grandchild. He was known as Prince Maurice of Battenbe
2 CONC rg throughout his life, as he died before the British Royal Family relinquished their German titles during World War I and changed their name to Mountbatten.
2 CONT
2 CONT The young Prince served in World War I as a lieutenant in the King's Royal Rifle Corps, and was killed in service in the Ypres Salient in 1914, age 23.  He is buried in Ypres Town Commonwealth War Graves Commission Cemetery.
2 CONT
2 CONT == Royal house ==
2 CONT
2 CONT *[http://www.geni.com/projects/House-of-Battenberg House of Battenberg] (Cadet branch of the House of Hesse-Darmstadt)
2 CONT
2 CONT Prince Maurice was the son of [http://www.geni.com/people/Maurice-of-Battenberg/6000000001504143245 Prince Henry of Battenberg]
2 CONT and [http://www.geni.com/people/Beatrice-Princess-of-Battenberg/6000000000693790112?through=6000000001504143245 Princess Beatrice of the United Kingdom]
2 CONT
2 CONT He died unmarried and without issue.
2 CONT
2 CONT Prince Maurice was a member of the Hessian princely Battenberg family and the extended British Royal Family, a grandson of Queen Victoria and her youngest grandchild. He was known as Prince Maurice of Battenberg throughout his lif
2 CONC e, as he died before the British Royal Family relinquished their German titles during World War I and changed their name to Mountbatten.
2 CONT
2 CONT == Biography ==
2 CONT
2 CONT Prince Maurice was born on 3 October 1891. He was given the name Maurice after his father Prince Henry of Battenberg and the great-grandfather, Count Maurice von Hauke, Victor after his grandmother the Queen, and Donald in honour 
2 CONC of Scotland, as he was born at Balmoral Castle. His father was Prince Henry of Battenberg, the son of Prince Alexander of Hesse and by Rhine and Julie Therese née Countess Hauke. His mother was Princess Henry of Battenberg (née Th
2 CONC e Princess Beatrice of the United Kingdom), the fifth daughter and the youngest child of Queen Victoria and Albert, Prince Consort.
2 CONT
2 CONT As his father was the product of a morganatic marriage, Prince Henry of Battenberg took his style of Prince of Battenberg from his mother, Countess Julia Hauke who was created Princess of Battenberg in her own right. As such, Maur
2 CONC ice was styled as His Serene Highness Prince Maurice of Battenberg from birth. In the United Kingdom, he was styled His Highness Prince Maurice of Battenberg under a Royal Warrant passed by Queen Victoria in 1886.
2 CONT
2 CONT The youngest of his four siblings, Maurice most resembled his father, who died when the Prince was only four, the same age his mother was when her own father died. He was his mother's favourite out of his brothers. He was educated
2 CONC  at Lockers Park Prep School in Hertfordshire.
2 CONT
2 CONT His elder sister Victoria Eugenie of Battenberg, married Alfonso XIII of Spain and was Queen Consort of Spain between 1906 and 1931.
2 CONT
2 CONT Maurice attended the prestigious Wellington College and was a member of the Benson House. 
2 CONT
2 CONT == Titles ==
2 CONT
2 CONT *His Highness Prince Maurice of Battenberg
2 CONT
2 CONT *within Germany: His Serene Highness Prince Maurice of Battenberg
2 CONT
2 CONT == Honours ==
2 CONT
2 CONT *KCVO: Knight Commander of the Royal Victorian Order
2 CONT
2 CONT == Links ==
2 CONT *[http://thepeerage.com/p10068.htm#i100676 The Peerage]
2 CONT *[http://www.geneall.net/U/per_page.php?id=384652 Geneall]
2 CONT *[http://www.findagrave.com/cgi-bin/fg.cgi?page=gr&GRid=12736468 Find a Grave]
2 CONT *[http://www.findagrave.com/cgi-bin/fg.cgi?GRid=6137142&page=gr Find a Grave(they are different!!)]
2 CONT *[http://www.hansdenyngre.dk/hans_uk/wizg40.htm#3864 Johann the Younger # 1973]
2 CONT *[http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Prince_Maurice_of_Battenberg Wikipedia]
2 CONT
2 CONT --------------------
2 CONT Prince Maurice of Battenberg, KCVO, was a member of the Hessian princely Battenberg family and the extended British Royal Family, the youngest grandchild of Queen Victoria. He was known as Prince Maurice of Battenberg throughout h
2 CONC is life, since he died before the British Royal Family relinquished their German titles during World War I and the Battenbergs changed their name to Mountbatten.
2 CONT
2 CONT Prince Maurice was born on 3 October 1891. He was given the name Maurice after his father Prince Henry of Battenberg and the great-grandfather, Count Maurice von Hauke, Victor after his grandmother the Queen, and Donald in honour 
2 CONC of Scotland, as he was born at Balmoral Castle. His father was Prince Henry of Battenberg, the son of Prince Alexander of Hesse and by Rhine and Julie Therese née Countess of Hauke. His mother was Princess Henry of Battenberg (née
2 CONC  The Princess Beatrice of the United Kingdom), the fifth daughter and the youngest child of Queen Victoria and Albert, Prince Consort.
2 CONT
2 CONT As he was the child of a morganatic marriage, Prince Henry of Battenberg took his style of Prince of Battenberg from his mother, Countess Julia Hauke who was created Princess of Battenberg in her own right. As such, Maurice was st
2 CONC yled as His Serene Highness Prince Maurice of Battenberg from birth. In the United Kingdom, he was styled His Highness Prince Maurice of Battenberg under a Royal Warrant passed by Queen Victoria in 1886. He was baptised in the Dra
2 CONC wing Room at Balmoral on 31 October 1891. His godparents were the Duchess of Connaught and Strathearn (represented by Queen Victoria), the Princess of Leiningen (represented by Princess Christian of Schleswig-Holstein), the Duke o
2 CONC f Clarence and Avondale (represented by Sir Henry Ponsonby), Prince Francis Joseph of Battenberg (represented by Sir Fleetwood Edwards) and the Hereditary Grand Duke of Hesse.
2 CONT
2 CONT The youngest of his four siblings, Maurice most resembled his father, who died when the Prince was only four, the same age his mother was when her own father died. He was his mother's favourite out of his brothers. He was educated
2 CONC  at Lockers Park Prep School in Hertfordshire.
2 CONT
2 CONT His elder sister Victoria Eugenie of Battenberg, married Alfonso XIII of Spain and was Queen Consort of Spain between 1906 and 1931.
2 CONT
2 CONT Maurice attended Wellington College and was a member of Benson House. Prince Maurice was made a Freemason in the Old Wellingtonian Lodge No. 3404 (the Lodge of the Old Wellingtonians) on 21 June 1912 and was installed Master of th
2 CONC e Twelve Brothers Lodge, No. 785 Southampton on 22 April 1914.
2 CONT
2 CONT The Prince served in World War I as a lieutenant in the King's Royal Rifle Corps, and was killed in service in the Ypres Salient in 1914. He is buried in Ypres Town Commonwealth War Graves Commission Cemetery. A memorial tablet to
2 CONC  him and his brother Leopold is in Winchester Cathedral.
