2 CONT The Prince George, Duke of Kent (George Edward Alexander Edmund; 20 December 1902 – 25 August 1942) was a member of the British Royal Family, the fourth son of George V and Mary of Teck. He held the title of Duke of Kent from 1934
2 CONC  until his death in 1942.
2 CONT
2 CONT The plane crashed while on a flight to Iceland during WWII. The aircraft was part of the 228th Squadron RAF.  The plane hit high ground at Eagle Rock in the Scottish Highlands in poor visibility. Possible navigation error but exac
2 CONC t cause unknown.  All 14 aboard killed.
2 CONT
2 CONT Among the dead was his Equerry, https://www.geni.com/people/Lieut-John-Lowther-MVO-RNVR/6000000011467041605?from_flash=1&fsession_id=1555086394852&through=6000000011467523492
2 CONT
2 CONT One of the trees for the Equerry in Ancestry.com states there was one survivor of the 15-person crew . . .
2 CONT
