2 CONT *[http://www.thepeerage.com/p2669.htm#i26681 The Peerage]
2 CONT *[http://www.geneall.net/D/per_page.php?id=5958 Geneall]
2 CONT *[http://www.hansdenyngre.dk/hans_uk/wizg53.htm#3189 Johann The Younger # 1824]
2 CONT *'''Wikipedia:''' [http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/William,_Prince_of_Wied English ] [http://de.wikipedia.org/wiki/Wilhelm_Adolph_Maximilian_V._zu_Wied Deutsch ] [http://nl.wikipedia.org/wiki/Wilhelm_Adolf_van_Wied Nederlands] 
2 CONT --------------------
2 CONT William V, Prince of Wied was a German officer and politician, elder son of Hermann, Prince of Wied. He was the father of William, Prince of Albania and brother of Queen Elisabeth of Romania.
2 CONT
2 CONT William was the second child and first son of Hermann, Prince of Wied (1814–1864), son of Johann August Karl, Prince of Wied and Princess Sophie Auguste of Solms-Braunfels, and his wife, Princess Marie of Nassau (1825–1902), daugh
2 CONC ter of William, Duke of Nassau and his first wife Princess Louise of Saxe-Hildburghausen. Through her mother he was descendant of William IV stadtholder of the Netherlands and George II of Great Britain.
2 CONT
2 CONT During the Austro-Prussian War in 1866, he was a lieutenant general staff of the 2nd Army. During 1870-71 he attended Franco-Prussian War.
2 CONT
2 CONT Between 1893 and 1897 he was the Imperial commissioner and military Chief of volunteer nurses in the army. In 1893 he was appointed as General of Infantry à la suite.
2 CONT
2 CONT Politically, William was a supporter of colonial policy. Between 1891 and 1892 he was chairman of the German anti-slavery committees. This funded include expeditions to unexplored areas in Africa. Since 1897, he was a member of th
2 CONC e Colonial Council. William was co-founder and from 1898 to 1901 President of the Navy League.
2 CONT
2 CONT Between 1875 and 1886 he was Marshal of Rhine Province parliament. He was from 1888 to 1894 and from 1899 to 1901 Chairman of the Rhine Province parliament. Since 1878, he was a member of the Prussian House of Lords. Which he was 
2 CONC president from 1897 to 1904.
2 CONT
2 CONT William married on 18 July 1871 in Wassenaar, Princess Marie of the Netherlands (1841–1910), younger daughter of Prince Frederick of the Netherlands (1792–1839) second son of William I of the Netherlands, and his wife, Princess Lo
2 CONC uise of Prussia (1808–1870), daughter of Frederick William III of Prussia.
2 CONT
2 CONT They had six children: William Frederick, Prince of Wied (27 June 1872 – 18 June 1945) married Princess Pauline of Württemberg (1877–1965), had issue. Prince Alexander of Wied (28 May 1874 – 15 January 1877) William, Prince of Alb
2 CONC ania (26 March 1876 – 18 April 1945) married Princess Sophie of Schönburg-Waldenburg (1885–1936), had issue. Prince Victor of Wied (7 December 1877 – 1 March 1946) married Countess Gisela of Solms-Wildenfels (1891–1976), had issue
2 CONC . Princess Louise of Wied (24 October 1880 – 29 August 1965) Princess Elisabeth of Wied (28 January 1883 – 14 November 1938)
