2 CONC wiki/Nicolas_II_de_Russie Français], [http://it.wikipedia.org/wiki/Nicola_II_di_Russia Italiano], [http://pl.wikipedia.org/wiki/Miko%C5%82aj_II_Romanow Polski ], [http://ru.wikipedia.org/wiki/%D0%9D%D0%B8%D0%BA%D0%BE%D0%BB%D0%B0%D
2 CONC 0%B9_II Русский], [http://zh.wikipedia.org/wiki/%E5%B0%BC%E5%8F%A4%E6%8B%89%E4%BA%8C%E4%B8%96_(%E4%BF%84%E7%BD%97%E6%96%AF 中文] [http://www.aol.com/article/2015/01/16/the-romanovs-final-days-as-seen-through-the-eyes-of-anastasia/21
2 CONC 130839/?ncid=txtlnkusaolp00001348 '''Lovely collectionof photos taken of & by the Tsar & his family''']
2 CONT *[http://www.youtube.com/watch?v=29ScRa7AEPA YouTube]
2 CONT
2 CONT '''Nicholas II''', Nikolay Alexandrovich Romanov and Mariya Feodorovna. Born on 18 May 1868 [Old Style 6 May] at Alexander Palace, Tsarskoye Selo, Saint Petersburg county, Russian Empire - died on July 17, 1918, at the Ipatiev Hou
2 CONC se, Yekaterinburg, Russian SFSR, age 50, executed by the Bolsheviks.
2 CONT
2 CONT Husband of [http://www.geni.com/people/Alexandra-Romanov-Tsarina-of-Russia/6000000000703434259?through=6000000000703639356 Alexandra Alexandra Fyodorovna Romanov], Tsaritsa (Tsarina - Americanized slang) of Russia.
2 CONT
2 CONT Children of Nicholas II and Alexandra:
2 CONT # Olga Nikolaevna Romanov, Grand Duchess of Russia;
2 CONT # Tatiana Nikolaievna Romanov, Grand Duchess of Russia;
2 CONT # Maria Nikolaevna Romanov, Grand Duchess of Russia;
2 CONT # Anastasia Nikolaevna Romanov, Grand Duchess of Russia;
2 CONT # Alexei Nikolaevich Romanov - Tsesarevich (prince) of Russia.
2 CONT
2 CONT Brother of:
2 CONT * Grand Duke Alexander Alexandrovich Romanov;
2 CONT * Grand Duke George Alexandrovich of Russia;
2 CONT * Xenia Alexandrovna Romanova, Grand Duchess of Russia;
2 CONT * Grand Duke Michael Alexandrovich of Russia Nikolaevna Romanov.
2 CONT
2 CONT Nicholas II was the last Emperor of Russia, Grand Prince of Finland, and titular King of Poland. His official title was Nicholas II, Emperor and Autocrat of All the Russias, and he is known as Saint Nicholas the Passion-Bearer by 
2 CONC the Russian Orthodox Church.
2 CONT
2 CONT Also known as:
2 CONT HIM Tsar Nicholas II of Russia, Saint Nicholas the Passion-Bearer, The Bloody, The Martyr, Romanov-Holstein-Gottorp, Nicholas II, Emperor and Autocrat of All the Russias. 
2 CONT
2 CONT Nicholas II abdicated following the February Revolution of 1917. Nicholas II; his wife, Alexandra Feodorovna; his son; his four daughters; and loyal servants were imprisoned and later executed by the Bolsheviks on the night of 16/
2 CONC 17 July 1918.  This led to the canonization of Nicholas II and his family as passion bearers, a category used to identify believers who, in imitation of Christ, endured suffering and death at the hands of political enemies, by the
2 CONC  Russian Orthodox Church within Russia, on 15 August 2000.
