2 CONT Name	Claude Stephen Jarrett
2 CONT Death	July 19 2010
2 CONT Published	July 20 2010,  Toronto, Ontario, Canada
2 CONT Published by	The Globe and Mail
2 CONT Obituary	'''JARRETT, Claude Stephen''' Died peacefully at Sunnybrook Health Sciences Centre on Monday, July 19, 2010 at the age of 90. Beloved husband of Lisa and the late Inga Jarrett. Loving father of Edward and Peter and devote
2 CONC d grandfather of Katelyn, Teddy, Daniel and Emilie. Also survived by his much loved sister Eva and her children in the U.K. Special friend of Daniel and Elizabeth Damov. He served with the British Army in Delhi, India in WWII. Cla
2 CONC ude pursued a successful career in Canada in commercial architecture, including notable buildings like the O'Keefe Centre and the Commerce Court. He was a wonderful and intellectually kind gentleman. A service will be held in the 
2 CONC HUMPHREY FUNERAL HOME - A.W. MILES CHAPEL, 1403 Bayview Avenue (south of Davisville Avenue) on Thursday, July 22 at 3:00 p.m. If desired, donations may be made to a charity of one's choice. Condolences and memories may be forwarde
2 CONC d through www.humphreymiles.com.
