2 CONT * 1 sibling, 12 servants
2 CONT
2 CONT '''From [https://www.findagrave.com/memorial/203314413/dorothy_alice_margaret_augusta_mack findagrave: Dorothy Alice Margaret Augusta Mack (née Grosvenor) (1890-1966)]'''
2 CONT
2 CONT * Name: Dorothy Alice Margaret Augusta Mack (née Grosvenor)
2 CONT * Born: Friday, 22 August 1890, Westminster, Greater London, England '''NOTE conflicts with current Stamford'''
2 CONT * Died: Tuesday, 11 January 1966 (aged 75), County Tipperary, Ireland
2 CONT * Buried: [St Mary the Virgin Churchyard, Church Road, Eccleston, Cheshire CH4 9HT 53.15701, -2.87926], England
2 CONT * Plot: [Plot 53.1584694, -2.8789028]
2 CONT * About: 
2 CONT
2 CONT Dorothy Alice Margaret Augusta Grosvenor was born in London on Friday, 22 August 1890. She was the second of three children born to Lord Henry George Grosvenor (1861-1914) and his first wife Dora Mina Erskine-Wemyss (1856-94). She
2 CONC  was a paternal granddaughter of Hugh Lupus Grosvenor, 1st Duke of Westminster (1825-99) and via her mother, a great-great-granddaughter of King William IV (1765-1837) and Dorothea Bland (1761-1816). 
2 CONT
2 CONT Dorothy married four times, her first three unions ending in divorce: 
2 CONT # Albert Edward Harry Meyer Archibald Primrose, Viscount Dalmeny [later 6th Earl of Rosebery and 2nd Earl of Midlothian] (1882-1974).
2 CONT # Robert Bingham Brassey
2 CONT # Chetwode Charles Hamilton Hilton-Greene (d. 1963)
2 CONT # Richard Herbert Mack (d.1967). 
2 CONT
2 CONT Following the accession of her brother, William Grosvenor (1894-1963), to the dukedom of Westminster, Dorothy was granted the rank and style of the daughter of a duke in the peerage of the United Kingdom.
2 CONT http://www.thepeerage.com/p967.htm#i9664
