1 NOTE
2 CONT
2 CONT George II (of Greece) (1890-1947), king of Greece (1922-23, 1935-41, 
2 CONT 1946-47), eldest son of King Constantine I, of the house of Glücksburg, 
2 CONT born at Tatoi, the royal estate near Athens. In 1921 he married Princess 
2 CONT Elizabeth of Romania (1894-1956). He succeeded to the throne after the 
2 CONT abdication of his father, but was himself deposed a year later, in 1923. 
2 CONT Returned to the throne by a plebiscite in 1935, George was, however, given 
2 CONT little authority, the actual power being in the hands of the military 
2 CONT dictator Ioannes Metaxas. The German invasion of Greece in 1941, during 
2 CONT World War II, caused him to take refuge first in Egypt and then in London, 
2 CONT where he established a government in exile. Following another plebiscite, 
2 CONT George returned to Greece in 1946. The following year he died and was 
2 CONT succeeded by his brother Paul I.
