1 OCCU Herzog von Braunschweig-Lüneburg, Prinz von Hannover, Prince of Great Britain and of Ireland
1 TITL Prinz
1 NOTE {geni:about_me} http://genealogics.org/getperson.php?personID=I00031307&tree=LEO
2 CONT
2 CONT BIOGRAPHY Born 18 March 1914 in Braunschweig, he was educated at Castle Salem, and later at the universities of Oxford, Berlin and Göttingen, and earned a degree in law. 
2 CONT
2 CONT On 31 August 1951 in Castle Marienburg near Hannover, he married Princess Ortrud von Schleswig-Holstein-Sonderburg-Glücksburg and they became the parents of six children. In 1953, after his father's death, he became the head of Ha
2 CONC nnoverian Royal Family. 
2 CONT
2 CONT It may have been his legal background that gave him a particular interest in the Act of Settlement passed by the British Parliament in 1701. In 1956 by persistence, he finally managed to establish in the British courts the right o
2 CONC f all non-Catholic descendants of the Electress Sophia von Hannover to British citizenship. This proved particularly important in the case of those descendants whose lands had been seized in eastern Europe after the was since they
2 CONC  were now able to establish claims for compensattion as British subjects. From; 'Queen Victoria's Descendants', by Marlene A. Eilers.
2 CONT
2 CONT *Ernst August Georg Wilhelm Christian Ludwig Franz Joseph Nikolaus Hannover, Prince(Prinz) von Hannover.
2 CONT *HRH Prince Ernest Augustus of the United Kingdom.
2 CONT *Herzog von Braunschweig-Lüneburg.
2 CONT *Abdicated as Prince of the United Kingdom on 28 March 1919.
2 CONT *Deprived of his British titles by an Order in Council.
2 CONT
