1 NOTE {geni:about_me} http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Victor_FitzGeorge-Balfour
2 CONT
2 CONT General Sir Robert George Victor FitzGeorge-Balfour, KCB, CBE, DSO, MC (15 September 1913 – 28 December 1994) was a General officer in the British Army.
2 CONT --------------------
2 CONT Robert George Victor FitzGeorge-Balfour was born on 15 September 1913 at Knightsbridge, London. 
2 CONT
2 CONT He was the son of Robert Shekelton Balfour and Mabel Iris FitzGeorge.
2 CONT
2 CONT Through his mother he was descendant of George III of the United Kingdom through his grandson Prince George, Duke of Cambridge and his mistress Sarah Fairbrother. 
2 CONT
2 CONT http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Victor_FitzGeorge-Balfour
2 CONT
2 CONT Full story of his life.
2 CONT
2 CONT He was given the name of Robert George Victor FitzGeorge-Balfour at birth. In 1922 his name was legally changed to Victor FitzGeorge-Balfour by deed poll.
2 CONT
2 CONT He was educated at Eton College, Windsor, Berkshire, England.
2 CONT
2 CONT He was educated at King's College, Cambridge University, Cambridge, Cambridgeshire, England.
2 CONT
2 CONT He gained the rank of officer in 1934 in the service of the Coldstream Guards.
2 CONT
2 CONT He was decorated with the award of the Military Cross (M.C.) (for service in Palestine) in 1939.
2 CONT
2 CONT He fought in the Second World War, serving in North Africa, Sicily and North West Europe.
2 CONT
2 CONT He gained the rank of Brigadier in 1942.
2 CONT
2 CONT He was invested as a Commander, Order of the British Empire (C.B.E.) in 1945.
2 CONT
2 CONT He gained the rank of Major in 1948 in the service of the 2nd Battalion, Coldstream Guards.
2 CONT
2 CONT He was decorated with the award of the Companion, Distinguished Service Order (D.S.O.) (for service in Malaya) in 1950.
2 CONT
2 CONT He was commander of the First Guards Brigade between 1958 and 1960.
2 CONT
2 CONT He was Deputy Director of Staff Duties between 1960 and 1962.
2 CONT
2 CONT He was Chief of Staff, Southern Commmand between 1962 and 1964.
2 CONT
2 CONT He held the office of Director of Military Operations between 1964 and 1967.
2 CONT
2 CONT He held the office of Senior Army Instructor in 1967.
2 CONT
2 CONT He was invested as a Knight Commander, Order of the Bath (K.C.B.) in 1968.
2 CONT
2 CONT He held the office of Vice-Chief of General Staff between 1968 and 1971.
2 CONT
2 CONT He retired from the military in 1977.3 He held the office of Deputy Lieutenant (D.L.) of West Sussex in 1977.
