1 NOTE {geni:about_me} Lieutenant THOMAS RICHARD CHETWYND BIRKIN, Dragoon Guards and R.F.C., killed on June 12th, aged 22, was the eldest son of Mr. and the Hon. Mrs. Stanley Birkin, of Park House, Mapperley, Nottingham. He was gazetted 
2 CONC to a Second Lieutenancy in the Yeomanry in the spring of 1914, being attached to a squadron Which was commanded by his uncle, Major H. L. Birkin. On the declaration of war, after training, he proceeded With his regiment to the Gal
2 CONC lipoli Peninsula, and was present at the action which took place after the landing at Suvla Bay. Later the regiment was ordered to another front, and in July, 1916, Mr. Birkin obtained a permanent commission in a Dragoon Guards re
2 CONC giment. Returning .to England, he Was attached to the Reserve Cavalry Depot for a few weeks, and then applied for service in the R.F.C., to which he Was temporarily transferred. He passed all his examinations, obtained his wings i
2 CONC n nine Weeks, and at the beginning of December, 1916, went abroad with a flying squadron. He came home on sick leave at the end of January, but returned to the Front three weeks ago. Mr. Birkin was the eldest grandson of Sir Thoma
2 CONC s Birkin, Bt., and a nephew of Viscount Chetwynd. His next brother. Second Lieutenant H. R. S. Birkin, is also serving abroad in the Flying Corps.
2 CONT
2 CONT Source: http://www.flightglobal.com/pdfarchive/view/1917/1917%20-%200625.html
2 CONT
2 CONT ===BIRKIN, T R C
2 CONT
2 CONT * Rank: Lieutenant
2 CONT * Date of Death: 12/06/1917
2 CONT * Regiment/Service: Royal Flying Corps 25th Sqdn. and 7th Dragoon Guards (Princess Royal's) 
2 CONT * Grave Reference: IV. F. 9. 
2 CONT * Cemetery: LAPUGNOY MILITARY CEMETERY
2 CONT * '''Additional Information:''' Eldest son of Sir T. Stanley Birkin, Bart., and the Hon. Lady Birkin, of Ruddington Grange, near Nottingham
2 CONT
2 CONT http://www.cwgc.org/find-war-dead/casualty/53797/BIRKIN,%20T%20R%20C
