1 NOTE {geni:about_me} Obituary, written by Karen Petersen, Herald Journal, Logan, Utah, 23 November 2008
2 CONT
2 CONT HYRUM, Utah, -- Derrall Courtney Petersen, our loving and much respected husband, father and grandfather, passed away Nov. 18 at his home in Hyrum after courageously enduring colon and pancreatic cancer for 6 ½ years. He was born 
2 CONC Feb. 4, 1930, to parents Leora Nielsen and Eugene Petersen and was raised in Hyrum. Derrall graduated from South Cache High School. He attended Utah State University, majoring in geology. Derrall served in the Korean War. He marri
2 CONC ed Karen Hawkins in 1955 in Logan; the marriage was later solemnized in the Logan LDS Temple.
2 CONT
2 CONT Derrall and Karen lived in Quincy, Washington for 2 ½ years, and then returned to Hyrum, where they have lived ever since. Derrall has been owner and operator of Monument Mountain Ranch for many years. He was recognized as Outstan
2 CONC ding Farmer in Box Elder County. He was employed for 25 years at Thiokol. He served as President of G&G Corp.
2 CONT
2 CONT Derrall took a lot of pride in his ranch and enjoyed the opportunity to teach his four sons good work ethics. He recently developed a stock water system, which will greatly enhance the property. This project was years in the proce
2 CONC ss, with final completion by employees Monday evening, only hours before Derrall passed away.
2 CONT
2 CONT Derrall’s passing will leave a vacuum for his knowledge and advice for family, friends, and associates.
2 CONT
2 CONT He owned property at Left Hand Fork in Blacksmith Fork Canyon and enjoyed maintaining and improving the area, fighting gophers and establishing a camping and recreation area, which has been enjoyed by family and friends.
2 CONT
2 CONT He was a faithful member of the LDS Church. He had a strong testimony of the Gospel. 
2 CONT
2 CONT He was responsible in his callings to serve, serving in the Sunday School presidency, activities committee, and as a high priest.
2 CONT
2 CONT He enjoyed associating with friends and co-workers. He loved spending winter months in Palm Springs, California, trips to Tucson and especially enjoyed visiting grandchildren. His hobbies were hunting for arrowheads, fossils, stud
2 CONC ying astronomy and jewelry making.
2 CONT
2 CONT Derrall is survived by his wife of 53 years, Karen; his four sons, Corey (Kathy), Mike (Ida), Jeff, Chris (Oana); 15 grandchildren; and three great-grandchildren. The grandchildren are Justin (Kenzee) and Jodi (Rich) Sorenson; Dar
2 CONC en, Brandon, Evan, Dylan, Benjamin, Daniel, Tyson Helms, Paige, Maggie, Conner, Courtney, Brett and Nick Ostler. He is survived by sister, Delone (Wes) Bailey, of Alamo California; brother, Dennis (Kaye) of St. George, Utah; siste
2 CONC rs-in-law Bara (Jay) Petersen and Betty (Doyle) Hawkins; and numerous nieces and nephews who have played an important role in Derrall’s live.
2 CONT
2 CONT He was preceeded in death by his mother, Leora Nielsen; father, Eugene; brother, Jay; sister, Rhea and brother-in-law, Douglas Borlase; and two brothers-in-law, Doyle and Gale Hawkins.
2 CONT
2 CONT Derrall's family wishes to acknowledge Andy Lee for his many years of employment and friendship.
2 CONT
2 CONT The family wishes to extend appreciation to Dr. Elizabeth Prystas, Dr. Leslee Ingersoll, Dr. Jeffrey Strong and Intermountain Hospice of Cache Valley for their loving expertise and care.
2 CONT
2 CONT Funeral Services will be held at noon Monday, Nov 24, 2008, in the Hyrum 7th Ward chapel, 245 N. Apple Drive. Friends may call from 6 to 8 p.m. Sunday at Allen-Hall Mortuary, 34 E. Center, Logan, and from 10:30 to 11:30 a.m. Monda
2 CONC y at the ward. Interment will be in Hyrum City Cemetery. Condolences and thoughts may be expressed to the family online at www.allenmortuaries.net.
