1 NAME Clyde Fae /Hurst/ II
2 GIVN Clyde Fae
2 NSFX II
2 _MARNM Hurst
1 SEX M
1 BURI
2 ADDR
3 CITY Logan
3 STAE Utah
1 BIRT
2 DATE 13 JAN 1920
2 ADDR
3 CITY Logan
3 STAE Utah
3 CTRY United States
1 DEAT
2 DATE 18 FEB 2014
2 PLAC Mendon, Utah
2 ADDR
1 NOTE {geni:about_me} 
2 CONT ===Obituary===
2 CONT On Tuesday morning, Feb. 18, 2014, Clyde F. Hurst passed away at his home in Mendon, Utah, of old age. He was born in Logan on Jan. 13, 1920, to Clyde and Pearl Hurst at his home on 5th North, where he spent his childhood up until
2 CONC  he was married. While at Logan High, he met his sweetheart and companion, Margene Schaub. They were married in March of 1942 in the Logan Temple and spent 68 years together. Margene passed away in December of 2010.
2 CONT
2 CONT Clyde grew up in the depression era and learned to work and do without as most did in those times. After high school he worked for the railroad in Nevada in the summers to earn money to go to Utah State. He graduated from college 
2 CONC and the ROTC program and was given a commission as a 2nd Lieutenant in the Army, and served for 4 years, in California, Hawaii and the islands of Peleliu.
2 CONT
2 CONT After the war Clyde went to dental school in Portland, Ore. Clyde graduated in 1949 and they returned home to Cache Valley and set up a home and dental practice. Over the years they have had homes in Logan, North Logan and Mendon.
2 CONC  They were blessed with five children: Clyde R. (Diane) of Kingman, Ariz., Gordon J.(Theresa, deceased) of Las Vegas, Kathleen Walbridge (Tom) of Mendon, Stanley E. (Linda) of Millville, and Edwin S. (Leslie) of North Logan. They 
2 CONC have 21 grandchildren and 44 great-grandchildren.
2 CONT
2 CONT Clyde has always been active in the LDS church and has held many positions. He has always had a strong testimony of the Church, of The Book of Mormon and tithing, and has been a great example of the gospel teachings. Clyde and Mar
2 CONC gene loved serving in the Hartford, Conn. Mission for 18 months.
2 CONT Clyde has always loved the out-of-doors, and over the years has participated in many outings such as hiking, fishing, hunting, skiing, riding horses and trips to Bear Lake.
2 CONT
2 CONT Being a great dentist was always a focus of his life, working until he was 75 years old. He developed an excellent reputation for his dental work and also for his long and dedicated service in the local, state and national dental 
2 CONC organizations.
2 CONT
2 CONT The family really appreciates all the care that was given to Clyde over the years by Holly Speth and Sarah Echols. He had a great affection for both of them.
2 CONT
2 CONT Funeral services will be held at noon Monday, Feb. 24, in the Mendon Stake Center, 460 S. 100 East in Mendon. A viewing will be from 6 to 8 p.m. Sunday at the Allen-Hall Mortuary, 34 E. Center St. in Logan and from 10:30 to 11:30 
2 CONC a.m., Monday, prior to the services, at the Stake Center. Military rites and interment will be held in the Logan City Cemetery. In lieu of flowers please donate to your ward missionary fund. Condolences may be sent to the family a
2 CONC t www.allenmortuaries.net. 
2 CONT
2 CONT Published in Logan Herald Journal from Feb. 22 to Feb. 23, 2014 - See more at: http://www.legacy.com/obituaries/hjnews/obituary.aspx?pid=169793315#sthash.odCLOLKN.dpuf
