1 NOTE Gustavus Adolphus VI of Sweden was the 3rd great grandson of the Empress Josephine through her son Eugene.  Gustavus was 4th great grandson (by adoption) to the Emperor Napoleon I (through his adopted daughter Stephanie Beauharnai
2 CONC s).  Gustavus was also descended from Count Foulke von Bernadotte - who had been Napoleon's General, and who defeated Napoleon at Waterloo, then became King of Sweden.  What a strange coindidance!.
1 NOTE He was educated at the universities of Uppsala and Oslo. He entered the 
2 CONT army in 1902, served with both the Swedish and Norwegian forces, and 
2 CONT obtained the rank of general in 1932. Known as a patron of the arts, 
2 CONT Gustav was a serious collector of Chinese art. He also won an 
2 CONT international reputation as a classical archaeologist, having worked in 
2 CONT the field in Greece, Cyprus, and Italy. Gustav was succeeded by his 
2 CONT grandson, King Carl XVI Gustaf.
1 NOTE OR "ADOLF"; KING OF SWEDEN; ALSO HAD 3 OTHER CHILDREN
