1 NOTE {geni:about_me} Princess Feodora zu Solms-Baruth (later Schenk and Auersperg; 5 April 1920 – 23 March 2006) was a German noblewoman and successful high jumper. 
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT She is best known for:
2 CONT Sports career: Feodora competed in the high jump and won bronze at the European Athletics Championships in Vienna in 1938. She also competed at the 1952 Helsinki Olympics representing Austria. At the German Championships, she won 
2 CONC gold in 1939 and several silver medals.
2 CONT Family and marriages:
2 CONT She was born in Baruth/Mark, the daughter of Count Friedrich zu Solms-Baruth and Princess Adelheid zu Schleswig-Holstein-Sonderburg-Glücksburg.
2 CONT She was married twice: first to Gert Schenk (1942–1957) and later from 1961 to Karl Adolf von Auersperg.
