1 NOTE {geni:about_me} Dagmar Louise Thyra Sophie Augusta Petra Castenskjold
2 CONT --------------------
2 CONT Dagmar Louise Thyra Sophie Augusta Petra Castenskiold passed away on 12 July 2013, 81 years old. She was the youngest child and only daughter of Princess Dagmar of Denmark and the noble Jørgen Castenskiold - and thus a first cousi
2 CONC n of King Frederik IX of Denmark, King Olav of Norway, Crown Princess Märtha of Norway and Queen Astrid of the Belgians. 
2 CONT
2 CONT She spent her childhood at Kongstedlund manor in Jutland, but growing up in the countryside with a noble and royal background had its downside. She and her siblings were easy targets for teasing and name-calling among the local ch
2 CONC ildren. Some of them thought they were taken to school by horse-drawn carriage, but the truth was they had to walk all the way, regardless of the weather. She didn’t like her long string of names, again maybe because it made her d
2 CONC ifferent from the other children. 
2 CONT
2 CONT While the Castenskiolds may have been exposed to prejudice in the countryside because of the royal connection, I think they experienced the opposite problem with certain royal relatives, who couldn’t forget that Princess Dagmar ha
2 CONC d married beneath her station. It can’t always have been easy. 
2 CONT
2 CONT The late Dagmar Castenskiold had three sons by her first husband Poul Bitsch. Tragically, both he and their eldest son died in car accidents - but Dagmar found happiness again with her second husband Ole Friis Larsen, who survives
2 CONC  her. 
2 CONT
2 CONT Although aware of her special background, she was an unassuming and down-to-earth woman. ”It was my mother who was high-born, not me”, she often said. She lived a quiet life out the spotlight and hardly ever took part in royal gat
2 CONC herings. In her later years she did, however, attend Queen Ingrid’s funeral and Empress Dagmar’s reburial service in Roskilde Cathedral.  Only one of her three brothers survives her - and he is the last grandchild of King Frederik
2 CONC  VIII. 
2 CONT
2 CONT The funeral service takes place at Jersie Church on 19 July.
2 CONT
2 CONT https://www.thepeerage.com/p6366.htm
