3 CONT The King George VI Memorial chapel is part of St George’s chapel at Windsor Castle, and was commissioned by Queen Elizabeth II in 1962 as a burial place for her father. George VI was originally interred in the royal vault at the c
3 CONC astle after his death in 1952 before being moved to the chapel.
