1 NOTE Duke of Edinburgh
1 NOTE He spent his childhood in England at the home of his uncle, Louis 
2 CONT Mountbatten, 1st earl Mountbatten of Burma, and began a naval career in 
2 CONT 1939, when he entered the Royal Naval College, Dartmouth. He served in 
2 CONT both the Mediterranean and Pacific theaters during World War II and 
2 CONT married the then Princess Elizabeth in 1947, at which time he was named 
2 CONT duke of Edinburgh; in 1957 he was created prince of the United Kingdom. 
2 CONT Prince Philip, an active advocate of sports, science, and education, has 
2 CONT made many goodwill trips throughout the world, both as representative of, 
2 CONT and in company with, Queen Elizabeth.
