1 NOTE {geni:about_me} Duke Georg Alexander of Mecklenburg
2 CONT
2 CONT Georg Alexander, Duke of Mecklenburg
2 CONT
2 CONT Full name 	Georg Alexander Andreas Karl Michael Peter Philipp Ignaz Maria
2 CONT
2 CONT Born 	August 21, 1921(1921-08-21)
2 CONT
2 CONT Birthplace 	Nice, France
2 CONT
2 CONT Died 	January 26, 1996 (aged 74)
2 CONT
2 CONT Place of death 	Mirow, Germany
2 CONT
2 CONT Wife 	Archduchess Ilona of Austria
2 CONT
2 CONT Offspring 	Elisabeth Christine, Marie Catherine, Irene, Georg Borwin
2 CONT
2 CONT Royal House 	Mecklenburg
2 CONT
2 CONT Father 	Duke Georg of Mecklenburg
2 CONT
2 CONT Mother 	Irina Raievskya
2 CONT
2 CONT Georg Alexander, Duke of Mecklenburg (German: Georg Alexander Herzog zu Mecklenburg; 27 August 1921  – 26 January 1996) was the head of the House of Mecklenburg-Strelitz from 1962 until his death.[1]
2 CONT
2 CONT Contents
2 CONT
2 CONT [hide]
2 CONT
2 CONT     * 1 Biography
2 CONT
2 CONT     * 2 Marriage and children
2 CONT
2 CONT     * 3 Ancestry
2 CONT
2 CONT     * 4 References
2 CONT
2 CONT     * 5 External links
2 CONT
2 CONT [edit] Biography
2 CONT
2 CONT Georg Alexander was born in Nice, France the eldest son of the then Count Georg of Carlow and his first wife Irina Raievskya (1892-1955). His father assumed the title Duke of Mecklenburg with the style Serene Highness following hi
2 CONC s adoption by the head of the House of Mecklenburg-Strelitz and his uncle Duke Charles Michael. The adoption of the title was confirmed by the head of the Imperial House of Russia, Grand Duke Cyril Vladimirovich on 18 July 1929 an
2 CONC d recognised on 23 December by Grand Duke Friedrich Franz IV of Mecklenburg-Schwerin.[2]
2 CONT
2 CONT With the death of Duke Charles Michael on 6 December 1934 his father succeeded as head of the Grand Ducal house of Mecklenburg-Strelitz and thus Georg Alexander became heir apparent. The grand ducal family lived at Remplin Castle 
2 CONC in Mecklenburg until it was destroyed in a fire in April 1940. During the Second World War both Georg Alexander and his father were interned by the Gestapo for a time.
2 CONT
2 CONT Duke Georg Alexander studied law in Freiburg before completing his studies in banking. On 18 December 1950 his fathers title was confirmed by the House of Mecklenburg-Schwerin and he then assumed the style of Highness.[2] Georg Al
2 CONC exander lived for a time in Ireland where he managed a number of properties. On returning to Germany he spent twenty years working for an advertising company.[3]
2 CONT
2 CONT On 6 July 1962 he succeeded his father as head of the Grand Ducal house of Mecklenburg-Strelitz.[1] In 1990 he moved to Mecklenburg and was given an apartment in the former grand ducal residence of Mirow Castle by the local govern
2 CONC ment and he was involved in its reconstruction.[4] Georg Alexander died in Mirow and was succeeded as head of the Grand Ducal house by his son Duke Georg Borwin.
2 CONT
2 CONT [edit] Marriage and children
2 CONT
2 CONT Duke Georg Alexander was married in Sigmaringen to Archduchess Ilona of Austria (b. 1927) civilly on 30 April 1946 followed by a religious ceremony on 30 April. Archduchess Ilona belongs to the Hungarian Palatine branch of the Hou
2 CONC se of Habsburg-Lorraine and is a granddaughter of Archduke Joseph August of Austria. Georg Alexander and Ilona had four children before divorcing on 12 December 1974.[5]
2 CONT
2 CONT Name 	Birth 	Notes
2 CONT
2 CONT Duchess Elisabeth Christine 	22 March 1947 	Married Alhard, Baron von dem Bussche-Ippenburg (b. 30 June 1947) civilly on 15 November 1974 in Ludenscheid and religiously on 3 May 1975 at Hohenzollern Castle. Had three daughters bef
2 CONC ore divorcing on 15 December 1997.
2 CONT
2 CONT Duchess Marie Catherine 	14 November 1949 	Married Wolfgang von Wasielewski (b. 15 December 1951) civilly on 17 March 1978 at Bonn and religiously on 15 July at Biengen. Has two children.
2 CONT
2 CONT Duchess Irene 	February 8, 1915 	Married Constantin Harmsen (b. 28 April 1954) civilly on 22 September 1979 at Mexico City and religiously at Biengen on 26 July 1980. Has two sons.
2 CONT
2 CONT Duke Georg Borwin 	May 31, 1956 	Married Alice Wagner (b. 2 August 1959) in Hinterzarten civilly on 24 December 1985 and religiously on 19 July 1986. Has three children and is the current head of the House of Mecklenburg-Strelitz.
2 CONT --------------------
2 CONT https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Georg_Alexander,_Duke_of_Mecklenburg
