1 NOTE {geni:about_me} Marriage and children[edit] On 26 April 1932, he married Lady Eileen Beatrice Forbes (1912–1993) a daughter of Bernard Forbes, 8th Earl of Granard and Beatrice Mills Forbes, an American socialite who was the daught
2 CONC er of Ogden Mills.
2 CONT
2 CONT They had four children:
2 CONT
2 CONT John Crichton-Stuart, 6th Marquess of Bute (27 February 1933 – 22 July 1993) Lord David Crichton-Stuart (27 February 1933 – 1977) Lord James Crichton-Stuart (17 September 1935 – 5 December 1982) Lady Caroline Moira Fiona Crichton-
2 CONC Stuart (born 7 January 1941) Interests[edit] The Marquess was an expert ornithologist; in 1931 he bought the islands of St Kilda to preserve them as a bird sanctuary, leaving them to the National Trust for Scotland in 1956.[2]
2 CONT
2 CONT In 1953, the Marchioness of Bute and Lady St David's Fund was set up to encourage and support women to train as nurses and midwives in south Wales.
