1 NOTE {geni:about_me} === Lord Rhidian Crichton-Stuart
2 CONT * Born on 4 June 1917.
2 CONT * Son of John Crichton-Stuart, 4th Marquess of the County of Bute and Augusta Mary Monica Bellingham.
2 CONT * Married Selina van Wijk, daughter of Frederick Gerth van Wijk, on 20 July 1939.
2 CONT * Died on 25 June 1969 at age 52.
2 CONT * Educated at Ampleforth College, Ampleforth, Yorkshire, and at Magdalene College, Cambridge University, Cambridge, Cambridgeshire
2 CONT * Captain in the Royal Artillery (RARO).
2 CONT * Royal Company of Archers in 1948.
2 CONT * British Delegate to the International Legislative Assembly, Tangier between 1953 and 1957.
2 CONT * Knight of Obedience, Sovereign Military Order of Malta. '''Children of Lord Rhidian Crichton-Stuart and Selina van Wijk'''
2 CONT * Frederick John Patrick Crichton-Stuart b. 6 Sep 1940, d. 14 Jun 2011
2 CONT * Mary Margot Patricia Crichton-Stuart b. 18 Mar 1942
2 CONT * Major Jerome Niall Anthony Crichton-Stuart b. 1 Jan 1948<br/>
2 CONT http://www.thepeerage.com/p2396.htm#i23953<br/>
2 CONT
2 CONT ----
2 CONT
2 CONT '''Lord Rhidian Crichton-Stuart'''
2 CONT
2 CONT From Wikipedia, the free encyclopedia
2 CONT
2 CONT This article needs additional citations for verification. Please help improve this article by adding citations to reliable sources. Unsourced material may be challenged and removed. (January 2017) (Learn how and when to remove thi
2 CONC s template message) Lord Rhidian Crichton-Stuart (4 June 1917 – 25 June 1969) was a son of John Crichton-Stuart, 4th Marquess of Bute and Augusta Crichton-Stuart, Marchioness of Bute.
2 CONT
2 CONT Rhidian Crichton-Stuart was educated at Ampleforth College and at Magdalene College, Cambridge. He gained the rank of Captain in the service of the Royal Artillery (RARO). He was admitted to Royal Company of Archers in 1948. He wa
2 CONC s a British member of the International Legislative Assembly of the Tangier International Zone from 1953 to 1956. He was a Knight of Obedience, of the Sovereign Military Order of Malta. He died on 25 June 1969, aged 52.
2 CONT
2 CONT Marriage/Children[edit] He married Selina Gerth van Wijk on 20 July 1939. They had the following children:
2 CONT
2 CONT Fra Frederik John Patrick Crichton-Stuart (born 6 September 1940, died 14 June 2011) Mary Margot Patricia Crichton-Stuart (born 18 March 1942) Major Jerome Niall Anthony Crichton-Stuart (born 1 January 1948) His eldest son, Freder
2 CONC ik (9 June 1940 - 14 June 2011), also known as Fra' Fredrik Crichton-Stuart, was Grand Prior of the Sovereign Military Order of Malta Grand Priory of England. He headed Una Voce (Scotland), part of the international body of Una Vo
2 CONC ce, of which he was president (2005–2006). Una Voce actively promotes and encourages the use of and petitions for wider indults in facilitating the traditional Tridentine Mass in the Catholic liturgy.[1]
2 CONT
2 CONT References[edit] Jump up ^ Obituary for Fra Frederik Crichton-Stuart, scotsman.com; accessed 26 March 2016. Links[edit] Profile, thepeerage.com; accessed 26 March 2016.
2 CONT
2 CONT https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Lord_Rhidian_Crichton-Stuart
