1 NOTE {geni:about_me} Editor of the Catholic Herald 1971-76, & 1982-84. Called to the Bar in 1952, but made his career as a writer.and translator, publishing some 30 biographies, mostly on Royal and Political characters and the Pope. He
2 CONC  was a former Research Fellow of S.Anne's College, Oxford, a Fellow of the Royal Society of Literature and Freeman of the City of London.  He lived most of his life at his family home, Chipping Camden, England.  Obituaries describ
2 CONC e him as a 'delightful character'.
