1 NOTE {geni:about_me} * https://www.familysearch.org/en/tree/person/details/P7GY-7X9
2 CONT
2 CONT * https://www.wikitree.com/wiki/Engelhardt-636
2 CONT
2 CONT * https://www.legacy.com/us/obituaries/name/owen-doonan-obituary?id=57720949
2 CONT
2 CONT * https://www.findagrave.com/memorial/280907290/owen-patrick-doonan
2 CONT
2 CONT Owen Patrick Doonan III, passed away peacefully on March 2, 2025. Owen was born in Boston on May 9, 1939. His parents were Owen P. Doonan, Jr. and Mary E. Doonan of Malden. He grew up in Malden, MA and graduated from Malden High S
2 CONC chool where he enjoyed playing hockey as goalie as a member of the Malden High Golden Rods. Owen continued playing hockey at Boston University and then transferred to the University of Miami, Florida. Owen served in the U.S Army a
2 CONC nd Army Reserves and continued in the State Army Reserves until 1968.
2 CONT
2 CONT Owen met his wife Mary (McCarte) in Boston. They were married in Attleboro and lived in Boston, Stoughton and Manchester, Connecticut, where he worked to set up several franchises in the newly blossoming franchise industry before 
2 CONC moving to Duxbury as a young family of six.
2 CONT
2 CONT As a member of Holy Family Church, Owen served as a member of the Finance Committee at the time of the building of the new church and taught classes in Religious Education for eighth grade and Confirmation. He especially enjoyed t
2 CONC he boys Confirmation retreats and living his Cursillo at the Retreat house at Stonehill  College in Easton.
2 CONT
2 CONT Owen suffered a serious stroke in April of1996 and battled back to live with his disabilities and advocated for disabled people, serving on several State and private committees Including Easter Seals, Mass Rehabilitation Commissio
2 CONC n and the Perkins Library.
2 CONT
2 CONT Our Family was blessed to have Owen home for Christmas with all of the family to celebrate with Owen and Mary's on their 61st wedding anniversary.
2 CONT
2 CONT He is survived by his loving wife, Mary Doonan. He is also survived by his son Owen P. Doonan, IV and his wife Nursel of Calabasas, California, his daughter Mary- Beth Doonan and her fiancé William Winchell of West Yarmouth Mass.,
2 CONC  his daughter Kathleen Webb and her husband Richard of Plymouth Mass, his son John Doonan and his wife Michelle of Kingston, Mass, and his grandchildren Kayla St. Michel and her husband Jeff, Samantha Mulvaney, Matthew Webb, Dylan
2 CONC  Doonan, Aidan Doonan and Neisa Santos.
2 CONT
2 CONT Visiting hours will be held on Friday, March 14th at the Shepherd Funeral Home, 216 Main St, Kingston from 3:00 to 7:00 pm. A Funeral mass will be held on Saturday, March 15th at Holy Family Church, Duxbury at 10:00 am. Burial ser
2 CONC vices will directly follow at Mayflower Cemetery in Duxbury. 
