1 NOTE {geni:about_me} 
2 CONT "James George Alexander Bannerman Carnegie, 3rd Duke of Fife (23 September 1929 – 22 June 2015) was the grandson Louise, Princess Royal, a daughter of King Edward VII of the United Kingdom. As a female-line great-grandson of a Bri
2 CONC tish sovereign, he did not carry out royal and official duties or receive any funds from the Civil List. He was the second cousin of Elizabeth II of the United Kingdom and Harald V of Norway. Through his maternal grandfather, he w
2 CONC as also a descendant of William IV of the United Kingdom and Dorothea Jordan."
2 CONT
2 CONT He succeeded as the 3rd Duke of Fife [UK 1900] on 26 February 1959.
2 CONT He succeeded as the 3rd Earl of Macduff, co. Banff [UK 1900] on 26 February 1959.
2 CONT He succeeded as the 12th Lord Carnegie of Kinnaird and Leuchars [S. 1633] on 16 February 1992.
2 CONT He succeeded as the 12th Earl of Southesk [S. 1633] on 16 February 1992.
2 CONT He succeeded as the 4th Baron Balinhard, of Farnell, Forfar [UK 1869] on 16 February 1992. 
2 CONT He succeeded as the 9th Baronet Carnegie, of Pittarrow, co. Kincardine [N.S. 1663] on 16 February 1992. 
2 CONT He succeeded as the 12th Lord Carnegie of Kinnaird [S., 1616] on 16 February 1992.
2 CONT
2 CONT =====================================================================================
