2 CONT
2 CONT Princess Alexandrine Irene of Prussia was the eldest daughter and fifth child of Wilhelm, German Crown Prince, and his wife, Duchess Cecilie of Mecklenburg-Schwerin. She was affected with Down Syndrome and attended the Trüpersche 
2 CONC Sonderschule, a school dedicated to the education of young women with special needs. Princess Alexandrine lived most of her later life in Bavaria, first in Pöcking and later near Lake Starnberg, where was visited regularly by her 
2 CONC family.
