1 NOTE He was educated at Anavryta, a preparatory school, and at Greek military 
2 CONT academies. He ascended the throne on March 6, 1964, upon the death of his 
2 CONT father. His brief reign was marked by political upheavals. Early in 1967 a 
2 CONT military coup deposed the existing government and established a ruling 
2 CONT junta. In December of that year the king failed in an attempt to overthrow 
2 CONT the junta, and he and his family thereafter lived in exile. In June 1973, 
2 CONT the Greek military government declared Constantine deposed and established 
2 CONT a republic, a fact approved in a national referendum after the restoration 
2 CONT of civilian government in 1974.
