1 NOTE She was educated at the universities of Copenhagen and Cambridge. She 
2 CONT married Henri Marie Jean André, comte de Laborde de Monpezat, a Frenchman 
2 CONT who was created Prince Henrik of Denmark.  On the death of her father, 
2 CONT Frederick IX, Margaret became the first queen to reign over Denmark since 
2 CONT Margaret I, more than five and a half centuries earlier. A new Danish 
2 CONT succession law had been enacted in 1953 to allow her ascension to the 
2 CONT throne.
