2 CONT
2 CONT His Majesty Juan Carlos I, King of Spain
2 CONT
2 CONT (Su Majestad Don Juan Carlos I, Rey de España)
2 CONT
2 CONT other titles claimed...
2 CONT
2 CONT King of Spain, Castile, Leon, Aragon, Two Sicilies, Jerusalem, Navarre, Granada, Mallorca, Toledo, Seville, Valencia, Galicia, Sardinia, Cordoba, Corsica, Menorca, Murcia, Jaen, Algarves, Algeciras, Gibraltar, Canary Islands, and 
2 CONC the Spanish East and West Indies and of the Islands and Mainland of the Ocean Sea, Archduke of Austria, Duke of Burgundy, Brabant, Milan, Athens, Neopatria, and Limburg, Count of Habsburg, Flanders, Tyrol, Roussillon, and Barcelon
2 CONC a, Lord of Biscay, Lord of Molina, 
2 CONT
2 CONT Family and private life
2 CONT Juan Carlos was married on 14 May 1962, to Princess Sophia of Greece and Denmark, daughter of King Paul of Greece, firstly in a Roman Catholic ceremony at the Church of St. Denis, followed by a Greek Orthodox ceremony at the Metro
2 CONC politan Cathedral of Athens. She converted from Greek Orthodoxy to Roman Catholicism. They have three children:
2 CONT
2 CONT # Infanta Elena, Duchess of Lugo (born 20 December 1963)
2 CONT # Infanta Cristina (born 13 June 1965)
2 CONT # King Felipe VI of Spain (born 30 January 1968)
2 CONT
2 CONT ==Links:==
2 CONT
