0 @N6000000005598973608@ NOTE he was also Duke of Strathearn, Earl of Dublin, and Admiral of the White
1 CONT
1 CONT Prince Henry Frederick, Duke of Cumberland and Strathearn From Wikipedia, the free encyclopedia.
1 CONT
1 CONT His Royal Highness Prince Henry Frederick, Duke of Cumberland and Strathearn (November 27, 1745 - September 18, 1790) was the sixth child of Frederick, Prince of Wales and Augusta of Saxe-Gotha, and a younger brother of King Georg
1 CONC e III.
1 CONT
1 CONT On March 4, 1767 the Duke of Cumberland allegedly married Olive Wilmot (later Mrs Payne), a commoner, in a secret ceremony. There reportedly was one child, Olivia Wilmot (1772-1834) from this relationship, though the duke's parent
1 CONC hood was never proven. A landscape painter and novelist, Olivia Wilmot married John Thomas Serres, 1759-1825, and later, controversially, assumed the style of Princess Olivia of Cumberland.
1 CONT
1 CONT The Duke's marriage to the commoner Lady Anne Horton (or Houghton) (1743-1808) on October 2, 1771 was the catalyst for the Royal Marriages Act 1772, which forbids any descendant of George II to marry without the monarch's permissi
1 CONC on. There were no children from this marriage. Lady Anne, though from a good family -- she was a daughter of Simon Luttrell, Earl of Carhampton, and the widow of Christopher Horton of Catton Hall -- seems to have been rather loose
1 CONC  with her favors, given one wag's comment that she was "the Duke of Grafton's Mrs Houghton, the Duke of Dorset's Mrs Houghton, everyone's Mrs Houghton."
0 @N6000000002322291984@ NOTE She married her cousin, Christian, in 1766, but he was insane. Her liasian
