0 @N6000000002188399732@ NOTE
1 CONT
1 CONT      King Friedrich Wilhelm II of Prussia, nephew and successor of King Friedrich II (Friedrich the Great). He had the power but lacked the ability of his distinguished predecessors. He joined the European coalition in support of 
1 CONC King Louis XVI and fought in the early campaigns of the French Revolutionary Wars. Financial difficulties and the revolt of 1794 in Poland against the Prussian and Russian occupiers of that country following the second partition o
1 CONC f Poland led King Friedrich Wilhelm II to make a separate peace with the French at Basel in 1795. Friedrich Wilhelm's extravagance left a ruined exchequer. He was a patron of the arts and an amateur cellist; Mozart dedicated three
1 CONC  string quartets to him. His son, Friedrich Wilhelm III, succeeded him.
0 @N6000000002240778444@ NOTE Under his reign, Prussia achieved considerable expansion, despite his lack of
1 CONT exceptional military and political gifts. He was intellectually receptive and
1 CONT devoted to the arts, but when he succeeded his uncle Frederick the Great as
1 CONT king, he was unable to perpetuate his uncle's system of personal government.
1 CONT His most notorious domestic measure was his "Religious Edict" of 1788, which
1 CONT gave legal recognition of toleration to a narrow Protestantism. Culturally,
1 CONT painting, architecture, theatre, & music (chamber music) flourished under him.
