1 CONC 832, the third version of the bill passed in both chambers, but only because William threatened to create enough new peerages to insure passage of the bill. The Reform Act of 1832 extended the voting franchise to middle class land
1 CONC  owners and became the basis for further acts which eventually enfranchised all adult subjects.
