1 CONT militia clash at Lexington, starting the American Revolution. In 1776, the
1 CONT Continential Congress adopts the Declaration of Independence and the Stars
1 CONT and Strips for the American flag. In 1780, the Derby horse race is
1 CONT established in England. In 1781, the British, under Cornwallis, surrender to
1 CONT the Americans at Yorktown. In 1782, peace talks open in Paris.
