0 @N6000000002188395245@ NOTE
1 CONT
1 CONT      Frederik, the eldest son of the future King Christian IX and Queen Luise, was born on June 3, 1843. When his father was chosen as heir to the Danish throne, Prince Frederik was taken out of his public school and was put in ch
1 CONC arge of a private tutor. In October 1863, he went to Oxford for a year of study, but he had to return home at his father accesion to the throne, to take up his duties as Crown Prince; Frederik became a member of his father's Priva
1 CONC te Council. He took part in the War against Prussia in 1864. In 1891 he was named inspector general of the Army.
1 CONT    Prince Frederik was affable assured and elegant young man; he was frank and cheerful as all the memebers of King Christian's family.
1 CONT
1 CONT
1 CONT   Queen Luise wanted her eldest son married as brilliantly as her two daughters, Alexandra and Dagmar had. Quuen Victoria had two yet unmarried daughters, Helena and Louise, and Luise tried to married Frederik to one of them, but 
1 CONC the British Queen didn't want her daughters to marry the heir of a foreigner crown, who could take them away from her, she wanted for them some German princeling who could be able to set his home in England besides her. Moreover, 
1 CONC Victoria had always been pro-German and another Danish alliance (Frederik' sister, Alexandra, had married Victoria's eledst son, the Prince of Wales), would not be propper for her German interests. So Queen Luise had to look up fo
1 CONC r another wife for her son. In July 1868, Frederik became engaged to the seventeen-year-old only daughter of King Charles XV of Sweden, Princess Lovisa. Princess Lovisa's family was somehow ralted to Napoleon Buonaparte. She belon
1 CONC ged to the Bernadotte dynasty, which ruled in Sweden since 1818. The founder was John Bernadotte, who had been one of Napoleon's generals, and who was elected King of Sweden with the name of Charles XIV.. He married Desiree Clary,
1 CONC  who had once had a love affaire with the French Emperor.   Charles XIV's son, Oscar I, married Josephine de Beauharnais, Princess of Leuchtenberg, grandddaughter of Napoleon's first wife, the Empress Josephine. King Oscar I and Q
1 CONC ueen Josephine were Princess Lovisa's grandparents.
1 CONT    Crown Prince Frederik and Princess Lovisa married in Stockholm on July 28, 1869. Lovisa was a shy and plain girlwith much formal manners; she had the nickname of "Swan". She was so pious that she fall in bigotry. Compared to Pr
1 CONC ince Frederik's sisters, Lovisa was dull and boring, but she was very rich, coming her fortune from her mother, Lovisa of the Netherlands. As the years passed, Prince Frederik found his wife so priggiish and solemn thaty he couldn
1 CONC 't avoid looking for some more frivoulous companies somewhere else. He had always an eye for pretty girls; nevertheless he devotedly fulfilled his marital duties. After a year of marrigae Lovisa gave birth to their first son and h
1 CONC eir, the future King Christian X of Denmark, and along the following twenty years, they had seven children more.
1 CONT    The old King Christian IX died in 1906 and Frederik at last acceded the throne as King Frederik VIII; he was already 63 years old. As King, he tried to identify his throne with all the progressive movements of the time. he saw 
1 CONC the need of popularize the monarchy and tried to achieve it by traveling all around the country and abroad, delivering eloquent speeches, supporting charities and fighting for the rights of the Danish people living in the German-r
1 CONC uled duchy of Schleswig. For this purpose he visited Kaiser Wilhelm II in Berlin establishing for the first time since the Schleswig-Holstein affair, a friendly relation with Germany. He gained a greater independence for Iceland a
1 CONC nd when he visited the island he was acclaimed as any other Danish king had been.
1 CONT    In 1912, King Frederik was suffering of a weak heart and he and his family went to the South of France in order to rest and recover. During the second week of May, the King, feeling much better, started his way back home. He an
1 CONC d his family stopped in Hamburg for some days and in the evening of May 14, King Fredrik went out for a walk by himself. While crossing the Gransemarky, he tottered, being help by a stranger, who resulted to be a doctor named Seel
1 CONC igmann. The King assured the man he was all right and continued his walk. After having giving a few steps, Fredrik collapsed. Dr.Seeligmann, helped by a policeman, put the King into a cab (they didn't know who he was) and told the
1 CONC  driver to take him to a hospital. King Frederik died in the cab. His unidentified body was taken to a mortuary. His family found him until four in the morning. King Frederik VIII's body was taken back to Copenhagen on board of th
1 CONC e Royal yacht Danneborg
0 @N6000000005599098222@ NOTE Frederik VIII (June 3, 1843 ? May 14, 1912), king of Denmark, eldest son of King Christian IX, was born at Copenhagen. As Crown Prince of Denmark he took part in the war of 1864 against Austria and Prussia, and subsequently assist
1 CONC ed his father in the duties of government, becoming king on Christian's death in January 1906. On July 28, 1869 Frederik married Lovisa of Sweden (October 31, 1851 - March 20, 1926), daughter of Carl XV, King of Sweden and Carl IV
1 CONC , King of Norway, by whom he had a family of four sons and four daughters.
1 CONT
1 CONT His eldest son Christian, crown prince of Denmark (September 26, 1870 - April 20, 1947), was married on April 26, 1898 to Alexandrine (December 24, 1879 - December 28, 1952), daughter of Friedrich Franz III, Grand-Duke of Mecklenb
1 CONC urg-Schwerin (March 19, 1851 - April 10, 1987); and his second son, Carl (August 3 , 1872 - September 21, 1957), who married his cousin Maud, daughter of Edward VII of the United Kingdom, became king of Norway as Haakon VII in 190
1 CONC 5.
1 CONT
1 CONT On his return journey from a trip abroad, Frederik VIII died in Hamburg.
1 CONT
1 CONT Frederick VIII of Denmark From Wikipedia, the free encyclopedia.
1 CONT
1 CONT Frederik VIII (June 3, 1843? May 14, 1912), king of Denmark, eldest son of King Christian IX, was born at Copenhagen. As Crown Prince of Denmark he took part in the war of 1864 against Austria and Prussia, and subsequently assiste
1 CONC d his father in the duties of government, becoming king on Christian's death in January 1906. On July 28, 1869 Frederik married Lovisa of Sweden (October 31, 1851 - March 20, 1926), daughter of Carl XV, King of Sweden and Carl IV,
1 CONC  King of Norway, by whom he had a family of four sons and four daughters.
1 CONT
1 CONT His eldest son Christian, crown prince of Denmark (September 26, 1870 - April 20, 1947), was married on April 26, 1898 to Alexandrine (December 24, 1879 - December 28, 1952), daughter of Friedrich Franz III, Grand-Duke of Mecklenb
1 CONC urg-Schwerin (March 19, 1851 - April 10, 1987); and his second son, Carl (August 3, 1872 - September 21, 1957), who married his cousin Maud, daughter of Edward VII of the United Kingdom, became king of Norway as Haakon VII in 1905
1 CONC .
1 CONT
1 CONT On his return journey from a trip abroad, Frederik VIII died in Hamburg
0 @N6000000006127645025@ NOTE Fredrik VIII, 1843-1912, dansk kung 1906 efter sin far Christian IX. I motsats till fadern godtog Fredrik helt det parlamentariska styrelsesättet. Gift med Karl XV:s dotter Lovisa (danska Louise), 1851-1926).Fredrik fick sin först
1 CONC a undervisning i en offentlig realskola, men fick sedan en privatlärare. Sjutton år gammal utbildade han sig till officer men tillbringade en kort tid (1863) även vid Oxfords universitet.I kriget 1864 följde han med general Hegerm
1 CONC ann Lindencrones division i Jylland. Alltifrån faderns tronbestigning i november 1863 hade han som kronprins säte i statsrådet och var flera gånger regent under dennes frånvaro, liksom han ett par gångervar truppernas befälhavare 
1 CONC under olika manövrer. Från år 1891 var han inspektör för armén och ordförande i general- kommissionen, och även som president i "Det geografiske selskapet" (från 1876) samt hedersledamot av "Videnskabernes selskab"deltog han fliti
1 CONC gt i sällskaps sammankomster. Han var en ivrig frimurare och visade alltid stort intresse för fångvård och andra sociala och humanitära institutioner.Den 15 juli 1868 förlovade han sig med Karl XV:s dotter, Lovisa Bernadotte, och 
1 CONC året därpå, den 28 juli 1869, firades bröllopet i Stockholms slottskapell. De fick med tiden barnen:1) Christian X 1870-19472) Carl 1872-1957 (senare kung i Norge med namn Haakon VII)3) Louise 1875-19064) Harald 1876-19495) Ingebo
1 CONC rg 1878-1958 (gift med den svenska prinsen Karl Bernadotte)6) Thyra 1880-1945 (ogift)7) Gustaf 1880-1944 (ogift)8) Dagmar 1890-1961I januari 1906 dog hans far, Christian (87), och Fredrik blev då kung vid 63 års ålder. Han behöll 
1 CONC de ministrarna som redan fanns i regeringen och följde det parlamentariska styrelsesätt, som hade vidtagits 1901. I september samma år (1906)besökte han Stockholm och i november samma år Berlin, i maj 1907 London och Paris. I juli
1 CONC  samma år gjorde han även en resa till Färöarna och Island samt besökte i december Oskar II:s begravning i Stockholm. De sista åren av sitt liv led han avhjärtfel. Fredrik dog i Hamburg 1912, på väg hem till Danmark från ett besök
1 CONC  i Italien, dit han rest inkognito som greve av Rosenborg. Enligt ett rykte skall han ha hittats, drabbad av slaganfall, i trappan till ett ökänt kärleksnäste i glädjekvarteren iS:t Pauli. Enligt en mer officiell version segnade h
1 CONC an ner på paradgatan Jungfernstieg vid Alster, sedan han druckit ett glas vin på en respektabel restaurang.
