0 @N6000000005599098194@ NOTE a.k.a.: King George I of Greece; George I, King of the Hellenes. He was assassinated in Salonika in 1913; Reign: 1863-1913; He was succeeded by his son, Constantine I. George was the first Greek monarch of the house of Glucksburg.
1 CONT
1 CONT George I of Greece From Wikipedia, the free encyclopedia.
1 CONT
1 CONT George I (December 24, 1845 - March 18, 1913) was king of Greece from 1863 to 1913
1 CONT
1 CONT He was born in Copenhagen, the second son of King Christian IX of Denmark and the brother of Alexandra of Denmark (consort of King Edward VII of the United Kingdom). He began his career in the Danish navy, and was elected King of 
1 CONC Greece on March 30, 1863 following the deposition of King Otto.
1 CONT
1 CONT The new king, now only 17 years old, quickly learned Greek in addition to his native Danish. During a trip to Russia to meet with his sister Dagmar (consort to Tsar Alexander III) he met Grand Duchess Olga, cousin of the Tsar, and
1 CONC  fell in love. They married in 1867.
1 CONT
1 CONT Together they had eight children: 1. Constantine (1868-1923), future king 2. Alexandria (1870-1891) 3. George (1869-1957) 4. Nicholas (1872-1938) 5. Mary (1876-1940) 6. Andrew (1882-1944) 7. Christopher (1888-1940) 8. Olga (died w
1 CONC hen three months old)
1 CONT
1 CONT When alone with his wife, he usually conversed in German. Their children were taught English by their nannies, and when talking with his children he therefore spoke mainly English.
1 CONT
1 CONT He ruled Greece with some success, overseeing the consolidation of Greek rule over Thessaly and Epirus and the putting down of rebellion in Crete. However, following the Balkan War which began in 1912, he was assassinated at Salon
1 CONC ika.
1 CONT
1 CONT External links A short illustrated profile of the King and his family <http://glucksburgstamps.school.dk/frame_george1greece.htm> (http://glucksburgstamps.school.dk/frame_george1greece.htm) A detailed profile in a site devoted to 
1 CONC the Greek Royal Family <http://www.greekroyalfamily.org/english/family_george1.html> (http://www.greekroyalfamily.org/english/family_george1.html)
0 @N6000000007329594085@ NOTE [Kopi av ROYALS.FTW]
1 CONT
1 CONT aka: King George I of Greece; George I, King of the Hellenes.   He was
1 CONT assassinated in Salonika in 1913; Reign: 1863-1913; He was succeeded by his
1 CONT son, Constantine I.  George was the first Greek monarch of the house of
1 CONT Glucksburg.
