0 @N6000000002322320117@ NOTE An admirer and patron of composer Richard Wagner, eccentric King Louis II
1 CONT brought his territories into the newly founded German Empire (1871) but
1 CONT concerned himself only intermittenly with affairs of state, preferring a life
1 CONT of increasingly morbid seclusion and developing a mania for extravagant
1 CONT building projects while worshipping the theatre and opera. One project called
1 CONT Neuschwanstein, was a fantastic fairy-tale castle precariously situated on a
1 CONT craig and decorated with scenes from Wagner's romantic operas.
