1 CONT honors ordered by Hitler. Note: "Kaiser" means German emperor. Thus ends the
1 CONT Prussian/German monarchs, followed by the Weimar Republic & The Third Reich.
0 @N6000000002188402153@ NOTE The Kaiser wanted "a place in the sun" for the German people. The problem was the only places left were in the shade. There was very little room left for new colonization in the early part of this century. Never the less the Kaise
1 CONC r built up the German military machine and under the Tirpitz Plan, built a naval fleet to rival that of Great Britain. The term "saber rattler" sums up his politics as well as his personality. Historian Barbara Tuchman put it well
1 CONC  when she referred to the Kaiser as "possessor of the least inhibited tongue in Europe".
1 CONT The Kaiser was born with a withered left arm (like FDR's polio, this defect was pretty well covered up and is visible in only a few photographs). This, together with having some tough footsteps in which to follow, led Wilhelm towa
1 CONC rds the military lifestyle. He loved his numerous uniforms and surrounding himself with the elite of German military society.  The Kaiser did not start the war. The Kaiser did not want the war. "Saber rattling" is one thing, a war
1 CONC  with the other major European powers is something very different indeed! The most that can be said is that the Kaiser did not do enough to try to control the actions of Austria-Hungary and prevent the outbreak of war. In the end 
1 CONC he accepted war.
0 @N6000000002244425391@ NOTE His father only reigned for 3 months, and he succeeded him to power. At the
1 CONT end of WW I, on November 10, a day before the Armistice was signed, he fled
1 CONT Germany and went to Holland to spend his remaining years in seclusion at
1 CONT Doorn Castle in the Netherlands. He remarried when his first wife died in
1 CONT 1921. Later, when he died on June 4, 1941, he was buried with full military
1 CONT honors ordered by Hitler. Note: "Kaiser" means German emperor. Thus ends the
1 CONT Prussian/German monarchs, followed by the Weimar Republic & The Third Reich.
0 @N6000000002322332576@ NOTE His father only reigned for 3 months, and he succeeded him to power. At the
1 CONT end of WW I, on November 10, a day before the Armistice was signed, he fled
1 CONT Germany and went to Holland to spend his remaining years in seclusion at
1 CONT Doorn Castle in the Netherlands. He remarried when his first wife died in
1 CONT 1921. Later, when he died on June 4, 1941, he was buried with full military
1 CONT honors ordered by Hitler. Note: "Kaiser" means German emperor. Thus ends the
1 CONT Prussian/German monarchs, followed by the Weimar Republic & The Third Reich.
