0 @N6000000001843182041@ NOTE Philip Mountbatten, Duke of Edinburgh, H.R.H.His birth name was Schleswig-Holtein-Sonderburg-Gluecksburg.  Hewas born Prince Philip of Greece and Denmark, the son of PrinceAndrew of Greece and Denmark and Princess (Victoria) Alice
1 CONC Elizabeth Julie Marie of Battenberg.  When he became anaturalized British subject, he took the surname Mountbatten andhe was known as Philip Mountbatten.  This is the GermanBattenberg, Anglicized, and switched around.  This was do
1 CONC nebecause of anti-German hysteria during WWI when George V decreedthat any German sounding name of the Royal family should bechanged and the King said that the family would take the surnameWindsor, rather than Sexe-Coburg or Wetti
1 CONC n as it had previouslydone.So, technically, Philip would be Philip Battenberg, Duke ofEdinburgh, Prince of the United Kingdom of Great Britain, KG,KT, OM, GBE, Prince Consort to the Queen.  In 1957 the queenconferred on him the ti
1 CONC tular dignity of a prince of the UnitedKingdom.Philip was ticked off when in 1952 the announcement was madethat the Royal Family would bear the name Windsor rather thanMountbatten.  This naming practice was slightly modified in 19
1 CONC 60when it was announced that the third generation of her male linedescendants should bear the surname Mountbatten-Windsor.
0 @N6000000001562994608@ NOTE Privately educated. After the death of her father, King George VI in 1952, she assumed various ceremonial duties, such as official tours of Commonwealth territories.  She was refused permission in 1955 to marry the divorced Royal 
1 CONC Air Force captain Peter Townsend (1914- ), a former member of her father's staff. a.k.a.: Princess Margaret, Countess of Snowdon.  Margaret and her husband, Anthony Armstron-Jones, Earl of Snowdon were divorced in 1978.  
1 CONT
1 CONT She was the last Royal born in England that required a Parliamentary witness for the Royal birth; the practice ended when her father decreed that there was no longer need for such anachronistic nonsense.  Margaret is 5'2" tall and
1 CONC  has blue eyes.  She supposedly has size 2 1/2 shoes.  She is a heavy smoker despite her doctor's warnings.  Margaret was a lively and talented girl, and was always considered to be the beauty of the family.
