1 CONT
1 CONT [edit] Early life
1 CONT
1 CONT Prince Philippos of Greece and Denmark was born on 10 June 1921 at Villa Mon Repos on Corfu, a Greek island in the Ionian Sea. His father was Prince Andrew of Greece and Denmark, the fourth son of Greece's King George I, who was o
1 CONC f partial Byzantine Greek descent, and Queen Olga of Greece. His mother was the former Princess Alice of Battenberg, elder daughter of the 1st Marquess of Milford Haven (formerly Prince Louis of Battenberg) and his wife, the forme
1 CONC r Princess Victoria of Hesse and by Rhine. Lady Milford Haven, through her mother, the Grand Duchess of Hesse and by Rhine (formerly Princess Alice of the United Kingdom), was a granddaughter of Queen Victoria. (As a descendant of
1 CONC  Queen Victoria, he is himself in line of succession to the British Throne, but very distantly.) Philip's mother Princess Alice, who ended her life as a Greek Orthodox nun and sheltered Jewish refugees in Athens during World War I
1 CONC I, was also a sister of Queen Louise of Sweden; George Mountbatten, 2nd Marquess of Milford Haven; and Louis Mountbatten, 1st Earl Mountbatten of Burma. He is currently the oldest living great-great grandchild of Queen Victoria, a
1 CONC s well as her second-oldest living descendant after Prince Carl Johan of Sweden.
1 CONT British Royal Family
1 CONT
1 CONT HM The Queen
1 CONT HRH The Duke of Edinburgh
1 CONT
1 CONT     * HRH The Prince of Wales
1 CONT       HRH The Duchess of Cornwall
1 CONT           o HRH Prince William of Wales
1 CONT           o HRH Prince Henry of Wales
1 CONT     * HRH The Duke of York
1 CONT           o HRH Princess Beatrice of York
1 CONT           o HRH Princess Eugenie of York
1 CONT     * HRH The Earl of Wessex
1 CONT       HRH The Countess of Wessex
1 CONT           o Viscount Severn
1 CONT           o Lady Louise Windsor
