1 CONT Nicholas II's first cousin.  Escaped the Bolsheviks and was the first Romanov
1 CONT to break his allegiance to Nicholas II.  In 1924, Cyril proclaimed himself
1 CONT "Tsarof all the Russias" and established his "court" in a village in Brittany.
1 CONT He died at sisty-two in 1938 in the American Hospital in Paris.  His son,
1 CONT Vladimir, (b. 1918) lives in Madrid and is considered head of the House of
1 CONT Romanov.  The Grand Duke Cyril was an officer in the Russian Imperial Navy and
1 CONT died while in exile.
