1 CONT Patrilineal descent
1 CONT
1 CONT Charles's patriline is the line from which he is descended father to son.
1 CONT
1 CONT Patrilineal descent is the principle behind membership in most royal houses, and can be traced back through the generations - which means that if Charles were to choose an historically accurate house name it would be Oldenburg/Sch
1 CONC leswig-Holstein-Sonderburg-Glucksburg,[citation needed] as all his male-line ancestors have been members.
1 CONT
1 CONT House of Oldenburg
1 CONT
1 CONT    1. Egilmar I of Lerigau, dates unknown
1 CONT    2. Egilmar II of Lerigau, d. 1142
1 CONT    3. Christian I of Oldenburg, d. 1167
1 CONT    4. Moritz of Oldenburg, d. 1209
1 CONT    5. Christian II of Oldenburg, d. 1233
1 CONT    6. John I, Count of Oldenburg, d. 1275
1 CONT    7. Christian III, Count of Oldenburg, d. 1285
