1 CONT     * Flag of Canada Commemorative Medal for the Centennial of Saskatchewan, 2005 [5]
1 CONT
1 CONT [edit] Military
1 CONT
1 CONT     * Sub-Lt, 1981-1983: Pilot, 820 NAS on HMS Invincible (including activity in the Falklands War)
1 CONT     * 1983-1984: Conversion to Lynx at RNAS Culdrose
1 CONT     * Lt, 1984-1986: Promoted to Lieutenant; pilot, 815 NAS on HMS Brazen
1 CONT     * 1987-1989: Helicopter Warfare Instructor, 702 NAS at RNAS Culdrose
1 CONT     * 1989-1991: Flight commander, 829 NAS on HMS Campbeltown
1 CONT     * Lt Cdr, 1992-1993: Army Command and Staff Course; promoted to Lieutenant-Commander
1 CONT     * 1993-1994: Captain, HMS Cottesmore
1 CONT     * 1994-1996: Senior Pilot, 815 NAS at RNAS Portland
1 CONT     * 1997-1999: Directorate of Naval Operations, MOD
1 CONT     * Cdr, 1999-2001: Promoted to Commander; appointed to Diplomacy Section of the Naval Staff
1 CONT     * Capt, 2005: Promoted to Captain (honorary)
1 CONT
1 CONT [edit] Honorary military appointments
1 CONT
1 CONT He holds the following military appointments:
1 CONT
1 CONT Flag of the United Kingdom United Kingdom
1 CONT
1 CONT     * Colonel-in-Chief, of the 9th/12th Royal Lancers (Prince of Wales's)
1 CONT     * Colonel-in-Chief, of The Royal Irish Regiment (27th (Inniskilling) 83rd and 87th and Ulster Defence Regiment)
1 CONT     * Colonel-in-Chief, of the Small Arms School Corps
1 CONT     * Colonel-in-Chief, of the Yorkshire Regiment (14th/15th, 19th and 33rd/76th Foot)
1 CONT
1 CONT     * Royal Colonel, of the Royal Highland Fusiliers, 2nd Battalion Royal Regiment of Scotland
1 CONT     * Honorary Air Commodore, Royal Air Force Lossiemouth.
1 CONT     * Commodore-in-Chief, Fleet Air Arm
1 CONT     * Admiral of the Sea Cadet Corps
1 CONT
1 CONT Prince Andrew's coat of arms
1 CONT Prince Andrew's coat of arms
1 CONT
1 CONT Flag of Canada Canada
1 CONT
1 CONT     * Colonel-in-Chief, of The Canadian Airborne Regiment (disbanded)
1 CONT     * Colonel-in-Chief, of The Princess Louise Fusiliers
1 CONT     * Colonel-in-Chief, of The Queen's York Rangers (1st American Regiment)
1 CONT     * Colonel-in-Chief, of The Royal Highland Fusiliers of Canada
1 CONT
1 CONT Flag of New Zealand New Zealand
1 CONT
1 CONT     * Colonel-in-Chief, of The Royal New Zealand Army Logistic Regiment
1 CONT
1 CONT [edit] Arms
1 CONT
1 CONT The Duke's personalized coat of arms are those of the Royal coat of arms of the United Kingdom with a label for difference: Quarterly (by quarters):
1 CONT
1 CONT     1st and 4th, Gules three Lions passant guardant in pale Or (England). (The first and fourth quarters display the three lions, representing England.)
1 CONT     2nd quarter is of a lion rampant within a Double Tressure floury counterflory Gules (Scotland). (The second quarter, displays a red lion in a yellow field with a double border coloured red, this represents Scotland.)
1 CONT     3rd, Azure a Harp Or stringed Argent (Ireland). (The third quarter shows a harp against a blue background, this represents Ireland.)
1 CONT
1 CONT The whole differenced by a Label of three points Argent the central point charged with an Anchor Azures. The anchor is in reference to his naval career.
1 CONT
1 CONT The arms are indentical to those his grandfather George VI used when still Duke of York.
1 CONT
