1 CONT [edit] Honorary military appointments
1 CONT The Princess Royal passes behind the Princess Anne Banner at a parade for the 75th anniversary of the Royal Australian Corps of Signals
1 CONT The Princess Royal passes behind the Princess Anne Banner at a parade for the 75th anniversary of the Royal Australian Corps of Signals
1 CONT The Princess Royal's Coat of Arms
1 CONT The Princess Royal's Coat of Arms
1 CONT The Princess Royal's Royal Standard
1 CONT The Princess Royal's Royal Standard
1 CONT
1 CONT Like other senior royals, The Princess Royal holds a number of honorary appointments in the British Armed Forces and those of several Commonwealth Realms. In 2002, she made history when she wore a Royal Navy uniform at the funeral
1 CONC  of her grandmother, Queen Elizabeth, the Queen Mother. She was the first non-reigning woman, who was also royal, to wear military uniform at a funeral.
1 CONT
1 CONT She is of the following regiments, corps, and branches:
1 CONT
1 CONT British
1 CONT
1 CONT     * Colonel-in-Chief, The King's Royal Hussars
1 CONT     * Colonel-in-Chief, The Worcestershire and Sherwood Foresters Regiment (29/45 Foot)
1 CONT     * Colonel-in-Chief, The Royal Corps of Signals
1 CONT     * Colonel-in-Chief, The Royal Logistic Corps
1 CONT     * Colonel-in-Chief, The Royal Army Veterinary Corps
1 CONT     * Commandant-in-Chief, The First Aid Nursing Yeomanry (Princess Royal's Volunteer Corps)
1 CONT     * Colonel, The Blues and Royals
1 CONT     * Royal Colonel, The Royal Scots Borderers, 1st Battalion Royal Regiment of Scotland
1 CONT     * Royal Colonel, The 52nd Lowland Regiment, 6th Battalion Royal Regiment of Scotland
1 CONT     * Rear Admiral and Chief Commandant for women, Royal Navy
1 CONT     * Honorary Air Commodore, RAF Lyneham
1 CONT     * Honorary Air Commodore, University of London Air Squadron
1 CONT     * Royal Honorary Colonel, University of London OTC
1 CONT     * Commodore-in-Chief, Portsmouth
1 CONT
1 CONT Commonwealth Realms
1 CONT
